<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 9.3. </span>The stratum <math id="S9.F3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{\mathcal{Y}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{\mathcal{Y}}</annotation></semantics></math> and the disks <math id="S9.F3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D,D_{1},D_{2},D_{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D,D_{1},D_{2},D_{3}</annotation></semantics></math>.</figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="S9.SS2.p13" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S9.SS2.p13.1" class="ltx_p">Recall from Subsection <a href="#S9.SS1" title="9.1. Stratifications compatible with a flow ‣ 9. Proof of the stratification lemma ‣ Packing stability and the subleading asymptotics of symplectic Weyl laws" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9.1</span></a> that the time <math id="S9.SS2.p13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau(q)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau(q)</annotation></semantics></math> it takes a flow line of <math id="S9.SS2.p13.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi^{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>φ</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi^{t}</annotation></semantics></math> starting at <math id="S9.SS2.p13.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q\in\Sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q\in\Sigma</annotation></semantics></math> to hit <math id="S9.SS2.p13.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma</annotation></semantics></math> again is bounded from above by <math id="S9.SS2.p13.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ρ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho</annotation></semantics></math>. Hence the disks <math id="S9.SS2.p13.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> are contained in the image of <math id="S9.SS2.p13.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi_{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mi>D</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi_{D}</annotation></semantics></math>. As explained above, <math id="S9.SS2.p13.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi_{D}^{-1}(D_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>ψ</mi><mi>D</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi_{D}^{-1}(D_{i})</annotation></semantics></math> is a perturbation of <math id="S9.SS2.p13.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C^{\infty}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>C</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C^{\infty}</annotation></semantics></math> size <math id="S9.SS2.p13.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(\sigma)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(\sigma)</annotation></semantics></math> of the disk <math id="S9.SS2.p13.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left\{0\right\}\times\left\{t_{i}\right\}\times B(z_{i},1/10)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo rspace="0.055em">}</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.055em">}</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\{0\right\}\times\left\{t_{i}\right\}\times B(z_{i},1/10)</annotation></semantics></math> for some <math id="S9.SS2.p13.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(t_{i},z_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(t_{i},z_{i})</annotation></semantics></math>. It follows from the bound <math id="S9.SS2.p13.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau\leq\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau\leq\rho</annotation></semantics></math> and the fact that the disks <math id="S9.SS2.p13.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> intersect <math id="S9.SS2.p13.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{C}_{\mathcal{Y}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{C}_{\mathcal{Y}}</annotation></semantics></math> that we can take <math id="S9.SS2.p13.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(t_{i},z_{i})\in(0,1/10)\times B(0,2/10)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(t_{i},z_{i})\in(0,1/10)\times B(0,2/10)</annotation></semantics></math>. Similarly, the preimage <math id="S9.SS2.p13.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi_{D}^{-1}(W_{D_{i}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>ψ</mi><mi>D</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi_{D}^{-1}(W_{D_{i}})</annotation></semantics></math> is the intersection with <math id="S9.SS2.p13.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[0,1]\times(-1,1)\times B(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[0,1]\times(-1,1)\times B(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math> of a perturbation of <math id="S9.SS2.p13.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[0,1]\times\left\{t_{i}\right\}\times B(z_{i},1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.055em">}</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[0,1]\times\left\{t_{i}\right\}\times B(z_{i},1)</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="S9.SS2.p13.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C^{\infty}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>C</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C^{\infty}</annotation></semantics></math> size <math id="S9.SS2.p13.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(\sigma)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(\sigma)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S9.SS2.p14" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S9.SS2.p14.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="S9.SS2.p14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{pr}_{23}:[0,1]\times(-1,1)\times B(0,1)\rightarrow\left\{0\right\}\times(-1,1)\times B(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>pr</mi><mn>23</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo rspace="0.055em">}</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{pr}_{23}:[0,1]\times(-1,1)\times B(0,1)\rightarrow\left\{0\right\}\times(-1,1)\times B(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math> denote the projection onto the second and third factor. For <math id="S9.SS2.p14.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in\left\{1,2,3\right\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in\left\{1,2,3\right\}</annotation></semantics></math>, let us now perturb <math id="S9.SS2.p14.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{D_{i}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{D_{i}}</annotation></semantics></math> such that</p>
<table id="S9.Ex25" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S9.Ex25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi_{D}^{-1}(W_{D_{i}})\cap N_{\varepsilon}(\operatorname{pr}_{23}^{-1}\psi_{D}^{-1}(\overline{C}_{\mathcal{Y}}))" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>ψ</mi><mi>D</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∩</mo><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>ε</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>pr</mi><mn>23</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>ψ</mi><mi>D</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi_{D}^{-1}(W_{D_{i}})\cap N_{\varepsilon}(\operatorname{pr}_{23}^{-1}\psi_{D}^{-1}(\overline{C}_{\mathcal{Y}}))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S9.SS2.p14.2" class="ltx_p">is contained in <math id="S9.SS2.p14.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[0,1]\times\left\{t_{i}\right\}\times B(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.055em">}</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[0,1]\times\left\{t_{i}\right\}\times B(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math>. Here <math id="S9.SS2.p14.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{\varepsilon}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>ε</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{\varepsilon}</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the <math id="S9.SS2.p14.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ε</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math>-neighbourhood as measured with respect to the standard metric on <math id="S9.SS2.p14.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[0,1]\times(-1,1)\times B(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[0,1]\times(-1,1)\times B(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math>. We can arrange this perturbation to be supported inside <math id="S9.SS2.p14.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{2\varepsilon}(\operatorname{pr}_{23}^{-1}\psi_{D}^{-1}(\overline{C}_{\mathcal{Y}}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>pr</mi><mn>23</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>ψ</mi><mi>D</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{2\varepsilon}(\operatorname{pr}_{23}^{-1}\psi_{D}^{-1}(\overline{C}_{\mathcal{Y}}))</annotation></semantics></math>. Moreover, we can make sure that the <math id="S9.SS2.p14.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C^{\infty}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>C</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C^{\infty}</annotation></semantics></math> size of this perturbation measured in the coordinate chart <math id="S9.SS2.p14.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi_{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mi>D</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi_{D}</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="S9.SS2.p14.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(\sigma)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(\sigma)</annotation></semantics></math> and in particular much smaller than <math id="S9.SS2.p14.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ε</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math>. Let us repeat this step for all top-dimensional strata <math id="S9.SS2.p14.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="S9.SS2.p14.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}</annotation></semantics></math> of type (S<a href="#S9.I2.i1" title="item 1 ‣ 9.1. Stratifications compatible with a flow ‣ 9. Proof of the stratification lemma ‣ Packing stability and the subleading asymptotics of symplectic Weyl laws" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>). Note that for two distinct such strata <math id="S9.SS2.p14.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S9.SS2.p14.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>C</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>, the modifications take place in disjoint regions because <math id="S9.SS2.p14.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{\mathcal{Y}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{\mathcal{Y}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S9.SS2.p14.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C^{\prime}_{\mathcal{Y}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C^{\prime}_{\mathcal{Y}}</annotation></semantics></math> are sufficiently far apart. We abbreviate the perturbed hypersurfaces by the same symbol <math id="S9.SS2.p14.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>D</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{D}</annotation></semantics></math>. Let us also perturb <math id="S9.SS2.p14.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\Sigma,\Sigma^{+})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\Sigma,\Sigma^{+})</annotation></semantics></math> by flowing the disk components <math id="S9.SS2.p14.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(D,D^{+})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>D</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>D</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(D,D^{+})</annotation></semantics></math> along the characteristic foliation on <math id="S9.SS2.p14.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left\{s_{-}\right\}\times Y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>{</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mo>−</mo></msub><mo rspace="0.055em">}</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\{s_{-}\right\}\times Y</annotation></semantics></math> such that they are contained in <math id="S9.SS2.p14.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>D</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{D}</annotation></semantics></math>. The modified surface pair and its induced stratifications are still denoted by <math id="S9.SS2.p14.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\Sigma,\Sigma^{+})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\Sigma,\Sigma^{+})</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S9.SS2.p14.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="S9.SS2.p14.m26" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{Y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{Y}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S9.SS2.p15" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S9.SS2.p15.1" class="ltx_p">For each disk component <math id="S9.SS2.p15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>D</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="S9.SS2.p15.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma</annotation></semantics></math>, let <math id="S9.SS2.p15.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>D</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{D}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the union of all characteristic leaves on <math id="S9.SS2.p15.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>D</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{D}</annotation></semantics></math> which intersect <math id="S9.SS2.p15.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>D</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="S9.SS2.p15.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{\Sigma}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>V</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{\Sigma}</annotation></semantics></math> be the union of all <math id="S9.SS2.p15.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>D</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{D}</annotation></semantics></math> as <math id="S9.SS2.p15.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>D</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D</annotation></semantics></math> ranges over the disk components of <math id="S9.SS2.p15.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma</annotation></semantics></math>. We define a diffeomorphism <math id="S9.SS2.p15.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha:[0,\sigma]\times\Sigma\rightarrow V_{\Sigma}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>σ</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha:[0,\sigma]\times\Sigma\rightarrow V_{\Sigma}</annotation></semantics></math> by declaring <math id="S9.SS2.p15.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha(s,p)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha(s,p)</annotation></semantics></math> to be the unique intersection point of the characteristic leaf starting at <math id="S9.SS2.p15.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math> with the slice <math id="S9.SS2.p15.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left\{s_{-}+s\right\}\times Y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mo>−</mo></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">}</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\{s_{-}+s\right\}\times Y</annotation></semantics></math>. Moreover, we define a map <math id="S9.SS2.p15.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau:V_{\Sigma}\rightarrow\mathbb{R}_{&gt;0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau:V_{\Sigma}\rightarrow\mathbb{R}_{&gt;0}</annotation></semantics></math> by</p>
<table id="S9.Ex26" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S9.Ex26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau(q)\coloneqq\inf\left\{t&gt;0\mid\varphi^{t}(q)\in V_{\Sigma}\right\}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">≔</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">inf</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>φ</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi></msub></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau(q)\coloneqq\inf\left\{t&gt;0\mid\varphi^{t}(q)\in V_{\Sigma}\right\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S9.SS2.p16" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S9.SS2.p16.1" class="ltx_p">We are now in a position to describe the top-dimensional strata of <math id="S9.SS2.p16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{X}</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="S9.SS2.p16.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math> be a top-dimensional stratum of <math id="S9.SS2.p16.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}</annotation></semantics></math> of type (S<a href="#S9.I2.i1" title="item 1 ‣ 9.1. Stratifications compatible with a flow ‣ 9. Proof of the stratification lemma ‣ Packing stability and the subleading asymptotics of symplectic Weyl laws" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>). We define the corresponding stratum <math id="S9.SS2.p16.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{\mathcal{X}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{\mathcal{X}}</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="S9.SS2.p16.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{X}</annotation></semantics></math> to be</p>
<table id="S9.Ex27" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S9.Ex27.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="C_{\mathcal{X}}\coloneqq\left\{\varphi^{t}(p)\mid p\in\alpha([0,\sigma]\times C),\kern 5.0pt0&lt;t&lt;\tau(p)\right\}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi></msub><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><msup><mi>φ</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>α</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>τ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{\mathcal{X}}\coloneqq\left\{\varphi^{t}(p)\mid p\in\alpha([0,\sigma]\times C),\kern 5.0pt0&lt;t&lt;\tau(p)\right\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S9.SS2.p16.2" class="ltx_p">We claim that <math id="S9.SS2.p16.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{C}_{\mathcal{X}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{C}_{\mathcal{X}}</annotation></semantics></math> is a symplectic cuboid. Indeed, let <math id="S9.SS2.p16.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>D</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D</annotation></semantics></math> denote the disk component of <math id="S9.SS2.p16.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma</annotation></semantics></math> containing <math id="S9.SS2.p16.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math>. Then it follows from our construction of the hypersurfaces <math id="S9.SS2.p16.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>D</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{D}</annotation></semantics></math> that</p>
<table id="S9.Ex28" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S9.Ex28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi_{D}^{-1}(\overline{C}_{\mathcal{X}})=[0,1]\times[0,T]\times\psi_{D}^{-1}(\overline{C})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>ψ</mi><mi>D</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>ψ</mi><mi>D</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi_{D}^{-1}(\overline{C}_{\mathcal{X}})=[0,1]\times[0,T]\times\psi_{D}^{-1}(\overline{C})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S9.SS2.p16.3" class="ltx_p">for some <math id="S9.SS2.p16.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>. Since <math id="S9.SS2.p16.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma^{-2}\psi_{D}^{*}\omega=\Omega+ds\wedge dt" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>ψ</mi><mi>D</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ω</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>∧</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma^{-2}\psi_{D}^{*}\omega=\Omega+ds\wedge dt</annotation></semantics></math> for some area form <math id="S9.SS2.p16.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Omega" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Omega</annotation></semantics></math> on <math id="S9.SS2.p16.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math> by Lemma <a href="#S9.Thmtheorem2" title="Lemma 9.2. ‣ 9.2. Stratification of thin products ‣ 9. Proof of the stratification lemma ‣ Packing stability and the subleading asymptotics of symplectic Weyl laws" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9.2</span></a>, we see that <math id="S9.SS2.p16.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{C}_{\mathcal{X}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{C}_{\mathcal{X}}</annotation></semantics></math> is a symplectic cuboid. It is conformally symplectomorphic to the cuboid <math id="S9.SS2.p16.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q(T,A)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q(T,A)</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="S9.SS2.p16.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the <math id="S9.SS2.p16.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Omega" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Omega</annotation></semantics></math>-area of <math id="S9.SS2.p16.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi_{D}^{-1}(\overline{C})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>ψ</mi><mi>D</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi_{D}^{-1}(\overline{C})</annotation></semantics></math>. Note that we can bound <math id="S9.SS2.p16.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S9.SS2.p16.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math> from above and below purely in terms of the universal constant <math id="S9.SS2.p16.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta</annotation></semantics></math>. This shows that we can find a universal compact set <math id="S9.SS2.p16.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{Q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒬</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{Q}</annotation></semantics></math> of symplectic cuboids such that every stratum <math id="S9.SS2.p16.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{C}_{\mathcal{X}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{C}_{\mathcal{X}}</annotation></semantics></math> associated to a stratum <math id="S9.SS2.p16.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math> of type (S<a href="#S9.I2.i1" title="item 1 ‣ 9.1. Stratifications compatible with a flow ‣ 9. Proof of the stratification lemma ‣ Packing stability and the subleading asymptotics of symplectic Weyl laws" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>) is conformally symplectomorphic to an element of <math id="S9.SS2.p16.m26" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{Q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒬</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{Q}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S9.SS2.p17" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S9.SS2.p17.1" class="ltx_p">Next, consider a top-dimensional stratum <math id="S9.SS2.p17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="S9.SS2.p17.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}</annotation></semantics></math> of type (S<a href="#S9.I2.i2" title="item 2 ‣ 9.1. Stratifications compatible with a flow ‣ 9. Proof of the stratification lemma ‣ Packing stability and the subleading asymptotics of symplectic Weyl laws" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>). Again, let <math id="S9.SS2.p17.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>D</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D</annotation></semantics></math> denote the disk component of <math id="S9.SS2.p17.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma</annotation></semantics></math> containing <math id="S9.SS2.p17.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math> and let <math id="S9.SS2.p17.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math> be the <math id="S9.SS2.p17.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Omega" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Omega</annotation></semantics></math>-area of <math id="S9.SS2.p17.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi_{D}^{-1}(C)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>ψ</mi><mi>D</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi_{D}^{-1}(C)</annotation></semantics></math>. Choose an area preserving parametrization <math id="S9.SS2.p17.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta:[0,\sigma A]\times[0,\sigma]\rightarrow\overline{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>σ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta:[0,\sigma A]\times[0,\sigma]\rightarrow\overline{C}</annotation></semantics></math> such that the boundary edges of <math id="S9.SS2.p17.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math> bordering strata of <math id="S9.SS2.p17.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}</annotation></semantics></math> of type (S<a href="#S9.I2.i3" title="item 3 ‣ 9.1. Stratifications compatible with a flow ‣ 9. Proof of the stratification lemma ‣ Packing stability and the subleading asymptotics of symplectic Weyl laws" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>) are given by <math id="S9.SS2.p17.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta(\left\{0\right\}\times[0,\sigma])" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo rspace="0.055em">}</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>σ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta(\left\{0\right\}\times[0,\sigma])</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S9.SS2.p17.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta(\left\{\sigma A\right\}\times[0,\sigma])" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">}</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>σ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta(\left\{\sigma A\right\}\times[0,\sigma])</annotation></semantics></math>. The boundary edges <math id="S9.SS2.p17.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta([0,\sigma A]\times\left\{0\right\})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta([0,\sigma A]\times\left\{0\right\})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S9.SS2.p17.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta([0,\sigma A]\times\left\{\sigma\right\})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta([0,\sigma A]\times\left\{\sigma\right\})</annotation></semantics></math> either border strata of <math id="S9.SS2.p17.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}</annotation></semantics></math> of type (S<a href="#S9.I2.i1" title="item 1 ‣ 9.1. Stratifications compatible with a flow ‣ 9. Proof of the stratification lemma ‣ Packing stability and the subleading asymptotics of symplectic Weyl laws" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>) or are contained in the boundary of <math id="S9.SS2.p17.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>D</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S9.SS2.p18" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S9.SS2.p18.1" class="ltx_p">Define a function <math id="S9.SS2.p18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f:[0,\sigma A]\times[0,\sigma]\rightarrow[0,\sigma]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>σ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>σ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f:[0,\sigma A]\times[0,\sigma]\rightarrow[0,\sigma]</annotation></semantics></math> by the formula</p>
<table id="S9.Ex29" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S9.Ex29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(x,y)\coloneqq\begin{cases}3x/A&amp;\text{if $0\leq x\leq\sigma A/3$}\\
\sigma&amp;\text{if $\sigma A/3\leq x\leq 2\sigma A/3$}\\
3\sigma-3x/A&amp;\text{if $2\sigma A/3\leq x\leq\sigma A$}.\end{cases}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mtext>if </mtext><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mi>σ</mi></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mtext>if </mtext><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>σ</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mtext>if </mtext><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(x,y)\coloneqq\begin{cases}3x/A&amp;\text{if $0\leq x\leq\sigma A/3$}\\
\sigma&amp;\text{if $\sigma A/3\leq x\leq 2\sigma A/3$}\\
3\sigma-3x/A&amp;\text{if $2\sigma A/3\leq x\leq\sigma A$}.\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S9.SS2.p18.2" class="ltx_p">We define</p>
<table id="S9.Ex30" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S9.Ex30.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="C_{\mathcal{X}}\coloneqq\left\{\varphi^{t}(p)\mid p\in\alpha\circ(\operatorname{id}_{\mathbb{R}}\times\beta)(\operatorname{int}D(f)),\kern 5.0pt0&lt;t&lt;\tau(p)\right\}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi></msub><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><msup><mi>φ</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>id</mi><mi>ℝ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>β</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>int</mi><mi>D</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>τ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{\mathcal{X}}\coloneqq\left\{\varphi^{t}(p)\mid p\in\alpha\circ(\operatorname{id}_{\mathbb{R}}\times\beta)(\operatorname{int}D(f)),\kern 5.0pt0&lt;t&lt;\tau(p)\right\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S9.SS2.p18.3" class="ltx_p">Here we recall that <math id="S9.SS2.p18.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D(f)\subset\mathbb{R}\times[0,\sigma A]\times[0,\sigma]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⊂</mo><mrow><mi>ℝ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>σ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D(f)\subset\mathbb{R}\times[0,\sigma A]\times[0,\sigma]</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the subgraph of <math id="S9.SS2.p18.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math> truncated at zero. See Figure <a href="#S9.F4" title="Figure 9.4 ‣ 9.2. Stratification of thin products ‣ 9. Proof of the stratification lemma ‣ Packing stability and the subleading asymptotics of symplectic Weyl laws" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9.4</span></a> for an illustration.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S9.F4" class="ltx_figure"><span id="S9.F4.pic1" class="ltx_picture ltx_centering" style="width:1.0pt;height:0.79230769pt;"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" version="1.1" width="1.33" height="1.05" overflow="visible"><g transform="translate(0,1.05) scale(1,-1)"><g transform="translate(0,0)"><g transform="translate(0,254.11) scale(1,-1)"><foreignObject width="320.80" height="254.11" overflow="visible"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2509.15390v1/x41.svg" id="S9.F4.pic1.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_landscape" width="333" height="264" aria-label="Refer to caption"></object></foreignObject></g></g><g transform="translate(1.23,0.16)"><g transform="translate(0,15.94) scale(1,-1)"><foreignObject width="16.47" height="11.16" overflow="visible"><Math mode="inline" tex="D" text="D" xml:id="S9.F4.pic1.m1">
                        <XMath xml:id="S9.F4.pic1.m1.1">
                          <XMTok font="italic" role="UNKNOWN">D</XMTok>
                        </XMath>
                      </Math></foreignObject></g></g></g></svg></span>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 9.4. </span>For some disk component <math id="S9.F4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>D</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="S9.F4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma</annotation></semantics></math>, the figure shows the intersection with <math id="S9.F4.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>D</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{D}</annotation></semantics></math> of all closures <math id="S9.F4.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{C}_{\mathcal{X}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{C}_{\mathcal{X}}</annotation></semantics></math> of strata of <math id="S9.F4.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{X}</annotation></semantics></math> associated to strata of <math id="S9.F4.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}</annotation></semantics></math> of types (S<a href="#S9.I2.i1" title="item 1 ‣ 9.1. Stratifications compatible with a flow ‣ 9. Proof of the stratification lemma ‣ Packing stability and the subleading asymptotics of symplectic Weyl laws" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>) and (S<a href="#S9.I2.i2" title="item 2 ‣ 9.1. Stratifications compatible with a flow ‣ 9. Proof of the stratification lemma ‣ Packing stability and the subleading asymptotics of symplectic Weyl laws" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>).</figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="S9.SS2.p19" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S9.SS2.p19.1" class="ltx_p">We claim that <math id="S9.SS2.p19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{C}_{\mathcal{X}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{C}_{\mathcal{X}}</annotation></semantics></math> is a perturbed symplectic frustum with cuts. Indeed, it follows from the way we adjusted the hypersurfaces <math id="S9.SS2.p19.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>D</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{D}</annotation></semantics></math> near the already constructed strata <math id="S9.SS2.p19.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{\mathcal{X}}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{\mathcal{X}}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="S9.SS2.p19.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>C</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> of type (S<a href="#S9.I2.i1" title="item 1 ‣ 9.1. Stratifications compatible with a flow ‣ 9. Proof of the stratification lemma ‣ Packing stability and the subleading asymptotics of symplectic Weyl laws" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>) that, for <math id="S9.SS2.p19.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y\in\left\{0,\sigma\right\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>σ</mi></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y\in\left\{0,\sigma\right\}</annotation></semantics></math>, a sufficiently small neighbourhood of</p>
<table id="S9.Ex31" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S9.Ex31.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left\{\varphi^{t}(p)\mid p\in\alpha\circ(\operatorname{id}_{\mathbb{R}}\times\beta)(D(f|_{[0,\sigma A]\times\left\{y\right\}}))\right\}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><msup><mi>φ</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>id</mi><mi>ℝ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\{\varphi^{t}(p)\mid p\in\alpha\circ(\operatorname{id}_{\mathbb{R}}\times\beta)(D(f|_{[0,\sigma A]\times\left\{y\right\}}))\right\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S9.SS2.p19.2" class="ltx_p">in <math id="S9.SS2.p19.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{C}_{\mathcal{X}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{C}_{\mathcal{X}}</annotation></semantics></math> looks eactly like a neighbourhood of a cut region in a perturbed symplectic frustum with cuts; see (B) in Figure <a href="#S7.F3" title="Figure 7.3 ‣ 7. Symplectic frusta ‣ Packing stability and the subleading asymptotics of symplectic Weyl laws" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7.3</span></a>. Moreover, after undoing these two cuts one obtains a perturbed symplectic frustum. Note that <math id="S9.SS2.p19.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{C}_{\mathcal{X}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{C}_{\mathcal{X}}</annotation></semantics></math> is conformally symplectomorphic to <math id="S9.SS2.p19.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi_{D}^{-1}(\overline{C}_{\mathcal{X}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>ψ</mi><mi>D</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi_{D}^{-1}(\overline{C}_{\mathcal{X}})</annotation></semantics></math> equipped with the symplectic form <math id="S9.SS2.p19.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Omega+ds\wedge dt" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>∧</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Omega+ds\wedge dt</annotation></semantics></math>. Since the hypersurfaces <math id="S9.SS2.p19.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi_{D}^{-1}(W_{D^{\prime}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>ψ</mi><mi>D</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><msup><mi>D</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi_{D}^{-1}(W_{D^{\prime}})</annotation></semantics></math> for other disk components <math id="S9.SS2.p19.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>D</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="S9.SS2.p19.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma</annotation></semantics></math> are contained in perturbations of <math id="S9.SS2.p19.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C^{\infty}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>C</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C^{\infty}</annotation></semantics></math> size <math id="S9.SS2.p19.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(\sigma)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(\sigma)</annotation></semantics></math> of hypersurfaces of the form <math id="S9.SS2.p19.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[0,1]\times\left\{t\right\}\times B(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mi>t</mi><mo rspace="0.055em">}</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[0,1]\times\left\{t\right\}\times B(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math>, the perturbed symplectic frustum underlying <math id="S9.SS2.p19.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi_{D}^{-1}(\overline{C}_{\mathcal{X}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>ψ</mi><mi>D</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi_{D}^{-1}(\overline{C}_{\mathcal{X}})</annotation></semantics></math> has, up to symplectomorphism, <math id="S9.SS2.p19.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C^{\infty}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>C</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C^{\infty}</annotation></semantics></math> distance <math id="S9.SS2.p19.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(\sigma)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(\sigma)</annotation></semantics></math> from an actual symplectic frustum <math id="S9.SS2.p19.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F=F(a,b,c)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F=F(a,b,c)</annotation></semantics></math>. Again we can bound <math id="S9.SS2.p19.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a,b,c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a,b,c</annotation></semantics></math> and also <math id="S9.SS2.p19.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c-b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c-b</annotation></semantics></math> from above and below by universal constants only depending on <math id="S9.SS2.p19.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta</annotation></semantics></math>. This implies that <math id="S9.SS2.p19.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>F</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F</annotation></semantics></math> is contained in some universal compact set <math id="S9.SS2.p19.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}</annotation></semantics></math> of symplectic frusta.</p>
</div>
<div id="S9.SS2.p20" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S9.SS2.p20.1" class="ltx_p">For each disk component <math id="S9.SS2.p20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>D</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="S9.SS2.p20.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma</annotation></semantics></math>, let <math id="S9.SS2.p20.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D\subset D^{0}\subset D^{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>⊂</mo><msup><mi>D</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><mo>⊂</mo><msup><mi>D</mi><mo>+</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D\subset D^{0}\subset D^{+}</annotation></semantics></math> be a disk whose boundary circle <math id="S9.SS2.p20.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\partial D^{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msup><mi>D</mi><mn>0</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\partial D^{0}</annotation></semantics></math> lies halfway between the boundary circles <math id="S9.SS2.p20.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\partial D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\partial D</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S9.SS2.p20.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\partial D^{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msup><mi>D</mi><mo>+</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\partial D^{+}</annotation></semantics></math>. Moreover, let <math id="S9.SS2.p20.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{D^{0}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>V</mi><msup><mi>D</mi><mn>0</mn></msup></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{D^{0}}</annotation></semantics></math> be the union of all characteristic leaves of <math id="S9.SS2.p20.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>D</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{D}</annotation></semantics></math> intersecting <math id="S9.SS2.p20.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D^{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>D</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D^{0}</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="S9.SS2.p20.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma^{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma^{0}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the union of all disks <math id="S9.SS2.p20.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D^{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>D</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D^{0}</annotation></semantics></math>. Similarly, let <math id="S9.SS2.p20.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{\Sigma^{0}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>V</mi><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mn>0</mn></msup></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{\Sigma^{0}}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the union of all <math id="S9.SS2.p20.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{D^{0}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>V</mi><msup><mi>D</mi><mn>0</mn></msup></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{D^{0}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Define <math id="S9.SS2.p20.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math> to be the union of <math id="S9.SS2.p20.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{\Sigma^{0}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>V</mi><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mn>0</mn></msup></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{\Sigma^{0}}</annotation></semantics></math> with all <math id="S9.SS2.p20.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{C}_{\mathcal{X}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{C}_{\mathcal{X}}</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="S9.SS2.p20.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math> ranges over strata of <math id="S9.SS2.p20.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}</annotation></semantics></math> of types (S<a href="#S9.I2.i1" title="item 1 ‣ 9.1. Stratifications compatible with a flow ‣ 9. Proof of the stratification lemma ‣ Packing stability and the subleading asymptotics of symplectic Weyl laws" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>) and (S<a href="#S9.I2.i2" title="item 2 ‣ 9.1. Stratifications compatible with a flow ‣ 9. Proof of the stratification lemma ‣ Packing stability and the subleading asymptotics of symplectic Weyl laws" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>). The remaining top-dimensional strata of <math id="S9.SS2.p20.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{X}</annotation></semantics></math> are given by the connected components of <math id="S9.SS2.p20.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="((0,\sigma)\times Y)\setminus A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∖</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">((0,\sigma)\times Y)\setminus A</annotation></semantics></math>. These connected components are in bijective correspondence with strata of <math id="S9.SS2.p20.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}</annotation></semantics></math> of type (S<a href="#S9.I2.i3" title="item 3 ‣ 9.1. Stratifications compatible with a flow ‣ 9. Proof of the stratification lemma ‣ Packing stability and the subleading asymptotics of symplectic Weyl laws" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>).</p>
</div>
<div id="S9.SS2.p21" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S9.SS2.p21.1" class="ltx_p">We claim that for each stratum <math id="S9.SS2.p21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="S9.SS2.p21.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}</annotation></semantics></math> of type (S<a href="#S9.I2.i3" title="item 3 ‣ 9.1. Stratifications compatible with a flow ‣ 9. Proof of the stratification lemma ‣ Packing stability and the subleading asymptotics of symplectic Weyl laws" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>), the closure of the corresponding stratum <math id="S9.SS2.p21.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{C}_{\mathcal{X}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{C}_{\mathcal{X}}</annotation></semantics></math> is symplectomorphic to a perturbed symplectic frustum with cuts, sitting inside <math id="S9.SS2.p21.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[0,\sigma]\times Y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>σ</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[0,\sigma]\times Y</annotation></semantics></math> upside down; see Figure <a href="#S9.F4" title="Figure 9.4 ‣ 9.2. Stratification of thin products ‣ 9. Proof of the stratification lemma ‣ Packing stability and the subleading asymptotics of symplectic Weyl laws" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9.4</span></a>. Consider a stratum <math id="S9.SS2.p21.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>C</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="S9.SS2.p21.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}</annotation></semantics></math> of type (S<a href="#S9.I2.i1" title="item 1 ‣ 9.1. Stratifications compatible with a flow ‣ 9. Proof of the stratification lemma ‣ Packing stability and the subleading asymptotics of symplectic Weyl laws" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>) such that <math id="S9.SS2.p21.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\overline{C}_{\mathcal{X}}^{\prime}\cap\overline{C}_{\mathcal{X}})\setminus V_{\Sigma}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>∩</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∖</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\overline{C}_{\mathcal{X}}^{\prime}\cap\overline{C}_{\mathcal{X}})\setminus V_{\Sigma}</annotation></semantics></math> is non-empty. Then the intersection of <math id="S9.SS2.p21.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{C}_{\mathcal{X}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{C}_{\mathcal{X}}</annotation></semantics></math> with a neighbourhood of <math id="S9.SS2.p21.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{C}_{\mathcal{X}}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{C}_{\mathcal{X}}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> looks like a neighbourhood of a cut region in a perturbed symplectic frustum with cuts; see (A) and (C) in Figure <a href="#S7.F3" title="Figure 7.3 ‣ 7. Symplectic frusta ‣ Packing stability and the subleading asymptotics of symplectic Weyl laws" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7.3</span></a>. Undoing all these cuts yields a perturbed symplectic frustum. As before, let <math id="S9.SS2.p21.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>D</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D</annotation></semantics></math> be the disk component of <math id="S9.SS2.p21.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma</annotation></semantics></math> containing <math id="S9.SS2.p21.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math> and consider <math id="S9.SS2.p21.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi_{D}^{-1}(\overline{C}_{\mathcal{X}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>ψ</mi><mi>D</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi_{D}^{-1}(\overline{C}_{\mathcal{X}})</annotation></semantics></math> equipped with <math id="S9.SS2.p21.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Omega+ds\wedge dt" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>∧</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Omega+ds\wedge dt</annotation></semantics></math>. As above, the perturbed symplectic frustum obtained by undoing all cuts of <math id="S9.SS2.p21.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi_{D}^{-1}(\overline{C}_{\mathcal{X}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>ψ</mi><mi>D</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi_{D}^{-1}(\overline{C}_{\mathcal{X}})</annotation></semantics></math> has, up to symplectomorphism, <math id="S9.SS2.p21.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C^{\infty}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>C</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C^{\infty}</annotation></semantics></math> distance <math id="S9.SS2.p21.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(\sigma)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(\sigma)</annotation></semantics></math> from an actual symplectic frustum <math id="S9.SS2.p21.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>F</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F</annotation></semantics></math>, which can be taken to be contained in a universal compact set <math id="S9.SS2.p21.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}</annotation></semantics></math> of symplectic frusta. This concludes the proof of Lemma <a href="#S8.Thmtheorem1" title="Lemma 8.1. ‣ 8. Proof of ellipsoid embedding stability ‣ Packing stability and the subleading asymptotics of symplectic Weyl laws" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8.1</span></a>. ∎</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S10" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">10. </span>Bounding the subleading asymptotics</h2>

<div id="S10.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S10.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The goal of this section is to prove Theorems <a href="#Thmintrothm4" title="Theorem D (Subleading asymptotics ECH). ‣ 1.4. Subleading asymptotics of symplectic Weyl laws ‣ 1. Introduction ‣ Packing stability and the subleading asymptotics of symplectic Weyl laws" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D</span></a>, <a href="#Thmintrothm5" title="Theorem E (Subleading asymptotics PFH). ‣ 1.4. Subleading asymptotics of symplectic Weyl laws ‣ 1. Introduction ‣ Packing stability and the subleading asymptotics of symplectic Weyl laws" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">E</span></a>, and <a href="#Thmintrothm6" title="Theorem F (Subleading asymptotics link spectral invariants). ‣ 1.4. Subleading asymptotics of symplectic Weyl laws ‣ 1. Introduction ‣ Packing stability and the subleading asymptotics of symplectic Weyl laws" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">F</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S10.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof of Theorem <a href="#Thmintrothm4" title="Theorem D (Subleading asymptotics ECH). ‣ 1.4. Subleading asymptotics of symplectic Weyl laws ‣ 1. Introduction ‣ Packing stability and the subleading asymptotics of symplectic Weyl laws" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D</span></a>.</h6>
<div id="S10.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S10.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S10.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">The proof follows the same strategy as the original proof of the ECH Weyl law in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bibx56" title="" class="ltx_ref">Hut11a</a>]</cite>. We proceed in several steps.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S10.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S10.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="S10.p3.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Step 1:</em><span id="S10.p3.1.2" class="ltx_text"> We claim that the error terms are bounded for balls, i.e. <math id="S10.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e_{k}(B(a))=O(1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e_{k}(B(a))=O(1)</annotation></semantics></math>. Indeed, by <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bibx59" title="" class="ltx_ref">Hut22a</a>, Example 1.2]</cite>, we have</span></p>
<table id="S10.Ex1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S10.Ex1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\liminf_{k\rightarrow\infty}e_{k}(B(a))=-\frac{3}{2}a\qquad\text{and}\qquad\limsup_{k\rightarrow\infty}e_{k}(B(a))=-\frac{1}{2}a," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">lim inf</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:2em;" width="2em"></mspace><mtext>and</mtext><mspace style="width:2.167em;" width="2.167em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">lim sup</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\liminf_{k\rightarrow\infty}e_{k}(B(a))=-\frac{3}{2}a\qquad\text{and}\qquad\limsup_{k\rightarrow\infty}e_{k}(B(a))=-\frac{1}{2}a,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S10.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S10.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">which clearly implies that <math id="S10.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e_{k}(B(a))=O(1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e_{k}(B(a))=O(1)</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S10.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S10.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="S10.p4.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Step 2:</em><span id="S10.p4.1.2" class="ltx_text"> We show that the error terms are bounded for all finite disjoint unions of balls. In fact, we show the following more general statement: Suppose that <math id="S10.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{1},\dots,X_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{1},\dots,X_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> is a finite collection of symplectic <math id="S10.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>4</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4</annotation></semantics></math>-manifolds such that <math id="S10.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e_{k}(X_{i})=O(1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e_{k}(X_{i})=O(1)</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="S10.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="S10.p4.m5" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="X\coloneqq\sqcup_{i}X_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo rspace="0em">≔</mo><mo lspace="0em">⊔</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mi>X</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X\coloneqq\sqcup_{i}X_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> be the disjoint union. Then we also have <math id="S10.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e_{k}(X)=O(1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e_{k}(X)=O(1)</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S10.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S10.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S10.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">Recall from <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bibx59" title="" class="ltx_ref">Hut22a</a>, Equation 1.4]</cite> that the ECH capacities of the disjoint union <math id="S10.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math> are given by</span></p>
<table id="S10.E1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(10.1)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S10.E1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{k}(X)=\max_{\sum_{i}k_{i}=k}c_{k_{i}}(X_{i})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><msub><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em" stretchy="true">∑</mo><mi>i</mi></msub></mstyle><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{k}(X)=\max_{\sum_{i}k_{i}=k}c_{k_{i}}(X_{i}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S10.p5.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S10.p5.2.1" class="ltx_text">Here the maximum is taken over all tuples of non-negative integers <math id="S10.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(k_{1},\dots,k_{n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(k_{1},\dots,k_{n})</annotation></semantics></math> whose sum is <math id="S10.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>. Set <math id="S10.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V\coloneqq\operatorname{vol}(X)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mi>vol</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V\coloneqq\operatorname{vol}(X)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S10.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{i}\coloneqq\operatorname{vol}(X_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mi>vol</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{i}\coloneqq\operatorname{vol}(X_{i})</annotation></semantics></math>. The desired statement follows immediately if we can verify that</span></p>
<table id="S10.E2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(10.2)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S10.E2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\max_{\sum\limits_{i}k_{i}=k}\sum\limits_{i}\sqrt{V_{i}k_{i}}=\sqrt{Vk}+O(1)\qquad(k\rightarrow\infty)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mmultiscripts><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>i</mi></munder><mprescripts></mprescripts><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><munder><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em" movablelimits="false" stretchy="true">∑</mo><mi>i</mi></munder></mstyle><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mrow></mrow></mmultiscripts><mo>⁡</mo><msqrt><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msqrt><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:2em;" width="2em"></mspace><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\max_{\sum\limits_{i}k_{i}=k}\sum\limits_{i}\sqrt{V_{i}k_{i}}=\sqrt{Vk}+O(1)\qquad(k\rightarrow\infty).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S10.p5.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S10.p5.3.1" class="ltx_text">Consider the function</span></p>
<table id="S10.Ex2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S10.Ex2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f:\mathbb{R}_{\geq 0}^{n}\rightarrow\mathbb{R}\qquad f(x_{1},\dots,x_{n})\coloneqq\sum\limits_{i}\sqrt{V_{i}x_{i}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:2em;" width="2em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">≔</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>i</mi></munder><msqrt><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f:\mathbb{R}_{\geq 0}^{n}\rightarrow\mathbb{R}\qquad f(x_{1},\dots,x_{n})\coloneqq\sum\limits_{i}\sqrt{V_{i}x_{i}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S10.p5.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="S10.p5.4.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="S10.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\in\mathbb{Z}_{&gt;0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>ℤ</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\in\mathbb{Z}_{&gt;0}</annotation></semantics></math>. It follows from a direct computation that the maximum of <math id="S10.p5.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math> subject to the constraint <math id="S10.p5.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum\limits_{i}x_{i}\leq k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>i</mi></munder><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum\limits_{i}x_{i}\leq k</annotation></semantics></math> is attained at the point <math id="S10.p5.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k/V\cdot(V_{1},\dots,V_{n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k/V\cdot(V_{1},\dots,V_{n})</annotation></semantics></math>. In particular, this implies that</span></p>
<table id="S10.E3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(10.3)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S10.E3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum\limits_{i}\sqrt{V_{i}\left\lfloor\frac{V_{i}k}{V}\right\rfloor}\leq\max_{\sum\limits_{i}k_{i}=k}\sum\limits_{i}\sqrt{V_{i}k_{i}}\leq\sum\limits_{i}\sqrt{\frac{V_{i}^{2}k}{V}}=\sqrt{Vk}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>i</mi></munder><msqrt><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>⌊</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mi>V</mi></mfrac><mo>⌋</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mmultiscripts><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>i</mi></munder><mprescripts></mprescripts><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><munder><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em" movablelimits="false" stretchy="true">∑</mo><mi>i</mi></munder></mstyle><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mrow></mrow></mmultiscripts><mo>⁡</mo><msqrt><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">≤</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>i</mi></munder><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mi>V</mi></mfrac></msqrt></mrow><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum\limits_{i}\sqrt{V_{i}\left\lfloor\frac{V_{i}k}{V}\right\rfloor}\leq\max_{\sum\limits_{i}k_{i}=k}\sum\limits_{i}\sqrt{V_{i}k_{i}}\leq\sum\limits_{i}\sqrt{\frac{V_{i}^{2}k}{V}}=\sqrt{Vk}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S10.p5.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="S10.p5.5.1" class="ltx_text">We compute</span></p>
<table id="S10.E4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(10.4)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S10.E4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum\limits_{i}\sqrt{V_{i}\left\lfloor\frac{V_{i}k}{V}\right\rfloor}=\sum\limits_{i}\sqrt{\frac{V_{i}^{2}k}{V}}+O(1)=\sqrt{Vk}+O(1)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>i</mi></munder><msqrt><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>⌊</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mi>V</mi></mfrac><mo>⌋</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>i</mi></munder><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mi>V</mi></mfrac></msqrt></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msqrt><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum\limits_{i}\sqrt{V_{i}\left\lfloor\frac{V_{i}k}{V}\right\rfloor}=\sum\limits_{i}\sqrt{\frac{V_{i}^{2}k}{V}}+O(1)=\sqrt{Vk}+O(1).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S10.p5.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="S10.p5.6.1" class="ltx_text">The desired identity (<a href="#S10.E2" title="In Proof of Theorem . ‣ 10. Bounding the subleading asymptotics ‣ Packing stability and the subleading asymptotics of symplectic Weyl laws" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10.2</span></a>) is immediate from (<a href="#S10.E3" title="In Proof of Theorem . ‣ 10. Bounding the subleading asymptotics ‣ Packing stability and the subleading asymptotics of symplectic Weyl laws" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10.3</span></a>) and (<a href="#S10.E4" title="In Proof of Theorem . ‣ 10. Bounding the subleading asymptotics ‣ Packing stability and the subleading asymptotics of symplectic Weyl laws" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10.4</span></a>).</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S10.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S10.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="S10.p6.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Step 3:</em><span id="S10.p6.1.2" class="ltx_text"> Let <math id="S10.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X\subset\mathbb{R}^{4}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>⊂</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mn>4</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X\subset\mathbb{R}^{4}</annotation></semantics></math> be a compact domain with smooth boundary. We show that the sequence of error terms <math id="S10.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e_{k}(X)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e_{k}(X)</annotation></semantics></math> is bounded from below. By Theorem <a href="#Thmintrothm1" title="Theorem A (Ball packing stability). ‣ 1.1. Ball packing stability ‣ 1. Introduction ‣ Packing stability and the subleading asymptotics of symplectic Weyl laws" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A</span></a>, ball packing stability holds for <math id="S10.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math>. Pick a positive integer <math id="S10.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="S10.p6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{n}(X)=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{n}(X)=1</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="S10.p6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> be the unique real number such that <math id="S10.p6.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\operatorname{vol}(B(a))=\operatorname{vol}(X)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>vol</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>vol</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\operatorname{vol}(B(a))=\operatorname{vol}(X)</annotation></semantics></math>. Then for every <math id="S10.p6.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b&lt;a" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b&lt;a</annotation></semantics></math>, the disjoint union of <math id="S10.p6.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> copies of <math id="S10.p6.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B(b)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B(b)</annotation></semantics></math> admits a symplectic embedding into <math id="S10.p6.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{int}(X)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>int</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{int}(X)</annotation></semantics></math>. By monotonicity of ECH capacities <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bibx59" title="" class="ltx_ref">Hut22a</a>, Equation 1.2]</cite>, we obtain the inequality</span></p>
<table id="S10.Ex3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S10.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{k}(\bigsqcup\limits_{i=1}^{n}B(b))\leq c_{k}(X)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><munderover><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">⨆</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{k}(\bigsqcup\limits_{i=1}^{n}B(b))\leq c_{k}(X)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S10.p6.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S10.p6.2.1" class="ltx_text">for all <math id="S10.p6.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b&lt;a" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b&lt;a</annotation></semantics></math>. Since the left hand side is continuous in <math id="S10.p6.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>b</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b</annotation></semantics></math>, the inequality continues to hold for <math id="S10.p6.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b=a" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b=a</annotation></semantics></math>. Using that <math id="S10.p6.m15" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\sqcup_{i}B(a)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>⊔</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sqcup_{i}B(a)</annotation></semantics></math> has the same volume as <math id="S10.p6.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math> and bounded error terms by Step 2, we conclude that the error terms <math id="S10.p6.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e_{k}(X)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e_{k}(X)</annotation></semantics></math> are bounded from below.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S10.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S10.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="S10.p7.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Step 4:</em><span id="S10.p7.1.2" class="ltx_text"> We show that the sequence of error terms <math id="S10.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e_{k}(X)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e_{k}(X)</annotation></semantics></math> is bounded from above for every compact domain <math id="S10.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X\subset\mathbb{R}^{4}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>⊂</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mn>4</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X\subset\mathbb{R}^{4}</annotation></semantics></math> with smooth boundary. Let <math id="S10.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B(A)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B(A)</annotation></semantics></math> be a large ball containing <math id="S10.p7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math> in its interior. By Theorem <a href="#Thmintrothm1" title="Theorem A (Ball packing stability). ‣ 1.1. Ball packing stability ‣ 1. Introduction ‣ Packing stability and the subleading asymptotics of symplectic Weyl laws" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A</span></a>, ball packing stability holds for <math id="S10.p7.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W\coloneqq B(A)\setminus\operatorname{int}(X)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∖</mo><mrow><mi>int</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W\coloneqq B(A)\setminus\operatorname{int}(X)</annotation></semantics></math>. Pick <math id="S10.p7.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="S10.p7.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{n}(W)=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{n}(W)=1</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="S10.p7.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> be the real number such that <math id="S10.p7.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\operatorname{vol}(B(a))=\operatorname{vol}(W)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>vol</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>vol</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\operatorname{vol}(B(a))=\operatorname{vol}(W)</annotation></semantics></math>. Then for every <math id="S10.p7.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b&lt;a" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b&lt;a</annotation></semantics></math>, the disjoint union of <math id="S10.p7.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> copies of <math id="S10.p7.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B(b)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B(b)</annotation></semantics></math> embeds into <math id="S10.p7.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{int}(W)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>int</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{int}(W)</annotation></semantics></math> and monotonicity implies the inequality</span></p>
<table id="S10.Ex4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S10.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{k}(X\sqcup\bigsqcup\limits_{i=1}^{n}B(b))\leq c_{k}(B(A))." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo rspace="0.055em">⊔</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">⨆</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{k}(X\sqcup\bigsqcup\limits_{i=1}^{n}B(b))\leq c_{k}(B(A)).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S10.p7.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S10.p7.2.1" class="ltx_text">Again, this inequality continues to hold for <math id="S10.p7.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b=a" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b=a</annotation></semantics></math>. The disjoint union formula (<a href="#S10.E1" title="In Proof of Theorem . ‣ 10. Bounding the subleading asymptotics ‣ Packing stability and the subleading asymptotics of symplectic Weyl laws" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10.1</span></a>) then implies that</span></p>
<table id="S10.E5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(10.5)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S10.E5.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="c_{k}(X)+c_{\ell}(\sqcup_{i}B(a))\leq c_{k+\ell}(B(A))" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mo lspace="0em">⊔</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>B</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{k}(X)+c_{\ell}(\sqcup_{i}B(a))\leq c_{k+\ell}(B(A))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S10.p7.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S10.p7.3.1" class="ltx_text">for all <math id="S10.p7.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math>. Set</span></p>
<table id="S10.Ex5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S10.Ex5.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="V_{1}\coloneqq\operatorname{vol}(X),\quad V_{2}\coloneqq\operatorname{vol}(\sqcup_{i}B(a)),\quad V\coloneqq\operatorname{vol}(B(A))=V_{1}+V_{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>≔</mo><mi>vol</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>≔</mo><mi>vol</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mo lspace="0em">⊔</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mi>V</mi><mo>≔</mo><mi>vol</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>B</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{1}\coloneqq\operatorname{vol}(X),\quad V_{2}\coloneqq\operatorname{vol}(\sqcup_{i}B(a)),\quad V\coloneqq\operatorname{vol}(B(A))=V_{1}+V_{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S10.p7.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="S10.p7.4.1" class="ltx_text">Since the error terms of <math id="S10.p7.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B(A)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B(A)</annotation></semantics></math> and of <math id="S10.p7.m17" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\sqcup_{i}B(a)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>⊔</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sqcup_{i}B(a)</annotation></semantics></math> are bounded by Steps 1 and 2, an upper bound on the error terms of <math id="S10.p7.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math> follows easily from inequality (<a href="#S10.E5" title="In Proof of Theorem . ‣ 10. Bounding the subleading asymptotics ‣ Packing stability and the subleading asymptotics of symplectic Weyl laws" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10.5</span></a>) if we can show that</span></p>
<table id="S10.Ex6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S10.Ex6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\inf_{\ell\geq 0}\sqrt{V(k+\ell)}-\sqrt{V_{1}k}-\sqrt{V_{2}\ell}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">inf</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></munder><msqrt><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mo>−</mo><msqrt><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msqrt><mo>−</mo><msqrt><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow></msqrt></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\inf_{\ell\geq 0}\sqrt{V(k+\ell)}-\sqrt{V_{1}k}-\sqrt{V_{2}\ell}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S10.p7.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="S10.p7.5.1" class="ltx_text">admits a finite upper bound independent of <math id="S10.p7.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>. This can be checked via an elementary computation in the same spirit as the one given in Step 2. We omit the details.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S10.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof of Theorem <a href="#Thmintrothm5" title="Theorem E (Subleading asymptotics PFH). ‣ 1.4. Subleading asymptotics of symplectic Weyl laws ‣ 1. Introduction ‣ Packing stability and the subleading asymptotics of symplectic Weyl laws" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">E</span></a>.</h6>
<div id="S10.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S10.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S10.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text">We closely follow the strategy of the proof of <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bibx45" title="" class="ltx_ref">EH</a>, Theorem 8.1]</cite> and adapt the notation from that paper.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S10.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S10.p9.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S10.p9.1.1" class="ltx_text">We begin by observing that is suffices to show the inequality</span></p>
<table id="S10.E6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(10.6)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S10.E6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{\sigma_{i}}(\phi,\gamma_{i},H_{+})-c_{\sigma_{i}}(\phi,\gamma_{i},H_{-})+\int_{\gamma_{i}}(H_{+}-H_{-})dt\geq d_{i}A^{-1}\int_{Y_{\phi}}(H_{+}-H_{-})dt\wedge\omega_{\phi}+O(1)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mo>+</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mo>−</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0em">∫</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mo>+</mo></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mo>−</mo></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0em">∫</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub></msub><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mo>+</mo></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mo>−</mo></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>∧</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{\sigma_{i}}(\phi,\gamma_{i},H_{+})-c_{\sigma_{i}}(\phi,\gamma_{i},H_{-})+\int_{\gamma_{i}}(H_{+}-H_{-})dt\geq d_{i}A^{-1}\int_{Y_{\phi}}(H_{+}-H_{-})dt\wedge\omega_{\phi}+O(1)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S10.p9.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S10.p9.2.1" class="ltx_text">for all Hamiltonians <math id="S10.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{\pm}\in C^{\infty}(Y_{\phi})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mo>±</mo></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msup><mi>C</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{\pm}\in C^{\infty}(Y_{\phi})</annotation></semantics></math>. Indeed, switching <math id="S10.p9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>H</mi><mo>+</mo></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{+}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S10.p9.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{-}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>H</mi><mo>−</mo></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{-}</annotation></semantics></math> in inequality (<a href="#S10.E6" title="In Proof of Theorem . ‣ 10. Bounding the subleading asymptotics ‣ Packing stability and the subleading asymptotics of symplectic Weyl laws" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10.6</span></a>) and multiplying the resulting inequality by <math id="S10.p9.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-1</annotation></semantics></math> yields the reverse inequality. Next, we observe that inequality (<a href="#S10.E6" title="In Proof of Theorem . ‣ 10. Bounding the subleading asymptotics ‣ Packing stability and the subleading asymptotics of symplectic Weyl laws" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10.6</span></a>) is invariant under shifting the Hamiltonians <math id="S10.p9.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{\pm}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>H</mi><mo>±</mo></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{\pm}</annotation></semantics></math> by constants. More precisely, if <math id="S10.p9.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{\pm}\in\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mo>±</mo></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{\pm}\in\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math> are real numbers, then inequality (<a href="#S10.E6" title="In Proof of Theorem . ‣ 10. Bounding the subleading asymptotics ‣ Packing stability and the subleading asymptotics of symplectic Weyl laws" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10.6</span></a>) holds for the pair <math id="S10.p9.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(H_{+},H_{-})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mo>+</mo></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mo>−</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(H_{+},H_{-})</annotation></semantics></math> if and only if it holds for the pair <math id="S10.p9.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(H_{+}+C_{+},H_{-}+C_{-})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mo>+</mo></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mo>+</mo></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mo>−</mo></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mo>−</mo></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(H_{+}+C_{+},H_{-}+C_{-})</annotation></semantics></math>. After replacing <math id="S10.p9.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>H</mi><mo>+</mo></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{+}</annotation></semantics></math> by <math id="S10.p9.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{+}+C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mo>+</mo></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{+}+C</annotation></semantics></math> for a sufficiently large constant <math id="S10.p9.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math>, we can assume that <math id="S10.p9.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{+}&gt;H_{-}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mo>+</mo></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mo>−</mo></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{+}&gt;H_{-}</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="S10.p9.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math> denote the symplectic cobordism between the graphs of <math id="S10.p9.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>H</mi><mo>+</mo></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{+}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S10.p9.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{-}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>H</mi><mo>−</mo></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{-}</annotation></semantics></math>. By Theorem <a href="#Thmintrothm1" title="Theorem A (Ball packing stability). ‣ 1.1. Ball packing stability ‣ 1. Introduction ‣ Packing stability and the subleading asymptotics of symplectic Weyl laws" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A</span></a>, ball packing stability holds for <math id="S10.p9.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math>. Pick <math id="S10.p9.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="S10.p9.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{N}(M)=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{N}(M)=1</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="S10.p9.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> be the real number such that <math id="S10.p9.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N\operatorname{vol}(B(a))=\operatorname{vol}(M)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>vol</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>vol</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N\operatorname{vol}(B(a))=\operatorname{vol}(M)</annotation></semantics></math>. Then for all <math id="S10.p9.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b&lt;a" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b&lt;a</annotation></semantics></math>, the disjoint union of <math id="S10.p9.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> copies of <math id="S10.p9.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B(b)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B(b)</annotation></semantics></math> admits a symplectic embedding into <math id="S10.p9.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{int}(M)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>int</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{int}(M)</annotation></semantics></math>. It follows from <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bibx45" title="" class="ltx_ref">EH</a>, Lemma 5.2]</cite> that for all non-negative integers <math id="S10.p9.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k_{i}\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k_{i}\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math> and for all <math id="S10.p9.m26" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b&lt;a" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b&lt;a</annotation></semantics></math> we have</span></p>
<table id="S10.E7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(10.7)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S10.E7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{\sigma_{i}}(\phi,\gamma_{i},H_{+})-c_{U^{k_{i}}\sigma_{i}}(\phi,\gamma_{i},H_{-})+\int_{\gamma_{i}}(H_{+}-H_{-})dt\geq c_{k_{i}}^{\operatorname{alt}}(\bigsqcup\limits_{j=1}^{N}B(b))." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mo>+</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mrow><msup><mi>U</mi><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mo>−</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0em">∫</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mo>+</mo></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mo>−</mo></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>c</mi><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mi>alt</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><munderover><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">⨆</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{\sigma_{i}}(\phi,\gamma_{i},H_{+})-c_{U^{k_{i}}\sigma_{i}}(\phi,\gamma_{i},H_{-})+\int_{\gamma_{i}}(H_{+}-H_{-})dt\geq c_{k_{i}}^{\operatorname{alt}}(\bigsqcup\limits_{j=1}^{N}B(b)).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S10.p9.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S10.p9.3.1" class="ltx_text">Here <math id="S10.p9.m27" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{k}^{\operatorname{alt}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>alt</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{k}^{\operatorname{alt}}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the elementary alternatives to ECH capacities defined in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bibx60" title="" class="ltx_ref">Hut22b</a>]</cite>, see Remark <a href="#S1.Thmtheorem2" title="Remark 1.2. ‣ 1.4. Subleading asymptotics of symplectic Weyl laws ‣ 1. Introduction ‣ Packing stability and the subleading asymptotics of symplectic Weyl laws" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1.2</span></a>. It is a consequence of <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bibx60" title="" class="ltx_ref">Hut22b</a>, Theorem 6]</cite> that the alternative capacities <math id="S10.p9.m28" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{k}^{\operatorname{alt}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>alt</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{k}^{\operatorname{alt}}</annotation></semantics></math> agree with the usual ECH capacities <math id="S10.p9.m29" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> on balls and disjoint unions of balls. Note that inequality (<a href="#S10.E7" title="In Proof of Theorem . ‣ 10. Bounding the subleading asymptotics ‣ Packing stability and the subleading asymptotics of symplectic Weyl laws" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10.7</span></a>) continues to hold for <math id="S10.p9.m30" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b=a" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b=a</annotation></semantics></math> by continuity.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S10.p10" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S10.p10.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S10.p10.1.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="S10.p10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math> be an integer such that all classes <math id="S10.p10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> are <math id="S10.p10.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>U</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U</annotation></semantics></math>-cyclic of order <math id="S10.p10.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math>. Such <math id="S10.p10.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math> exists by <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bibx37" title="" class="ltx_ref">CPPZ</a>]</cite>. We abbreviate</span></p>
<table id="S10.Ex7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S10.Ex7.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="V\coloneqq\operatorname{vol}(\sqcup_{j}B(a))=\operatorname{vol}(M)=\int_{Y_{\phi}}(H_{+}-H_{-})dt\wedge\omega_{\phi}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>≔</mo><mi>vol</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mo lspace="0em">⊔</mo><mi>j</mi></msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>vol</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><msub><mo rspace="0em">∫</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mo>+</mo></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mo>−</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>∧</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V\coloneqq\operatorname{vol}(\sqcup_{j}B(a))=\operatorname{vol}(M)=\int_{Y_{\phi}}(H_{+}-H_{-})dt\wedge\omega_{\phi}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S10.p10.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S10.p10.2.1" class="ltx_text">and set</span></p>
<table id="S10.Ex8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S10.Ex8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n_{i}\coloneqq\left\lfloor\frac{d_{i}^{2}V}{mA^{2}(d_{i}-g+1)}\right\rfloor\qquad\text{and}\qquad k_{i}=mn_{i}(d_{i}-g+1)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mo>⌊</mo><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mi>d</mi><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>⌋</mo></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:2em;" width="2em"></mspace><mtext>and</mtext><mspace style="width:2em;" width="2em"></mspace><mrow><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n_{i}\coloneqq\left\lfloor\frac{d_{i}^{2}V}{mA^{2}(d_{i}-g+1)}\right\rfloor\qquad\text{and}\qquad k_{i}=mn_{i}(d_{i}-g+1).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S10.p10.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S10.p10.3.1" class="ltx_text">By <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bibx45" title="" class="ltx_ref">EH</a>, Proposition 4.2(a)]</cite>, we have</span></p>
<table id="S10.Ex9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S10.Ex9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{U^{k_{i}}\sigma_{i}}(\phi,\gamma_{i},H_{-})=c_{\sigma_{i}}(\phi,\gamma_{i},H_{-})-mn_{i}A." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mrow><msup><mi>U</mi><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mo>−</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mo>−</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{U^{k_{i}}\sigma_{i}}(\phi,\gamma_{i},H_{-})=c_{\sigma_{i}}(\phi,\gamma_{i},H_{-})-mn_{i}A.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S10.p10.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="S10.p10.4.1" class="ltx_text">Using this, inequality (<a href="#S10.E7" title="In Proof of Theorem . ‣ 10. Bounding the subleading asymptotics ‣ Packing stability and the subleading asymptotics of symplectic Weyl laws" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10.7</span></a>) with <math id="S10.p10.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b=a" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b=a</annotation></semantics></math> can be rewritten as</span></p>
<table id="S10.E8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(10.8)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S10.E8.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="c_{\sigma_{i}}(\phi,\gamma_{i},H_{+})-c_{\sigma_{i}}(\phi,\gamma_{i},H_{-})+\int_{\gamma_{i}}(H_{+}-H_{-})dt\geq c_{k_{i}}(\sqcup_{j}B(a))-mn_{i}A." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mo>+</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mo>−</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><msub><mo rspace="0em">∫</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mo>+</mo></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mo>−</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>≥</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mo lspace="0em">⊔</mo><mi>j</mi></msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>m</mi><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{\sigma_{i}}(\phi,\gamma_{i},H_{+})-c_{\sigma_{i}}(\phi,\gamma_{i},H_{-})+\int_{\gamma_{i}}(H_{+}-H_{-})dt\geq c_{k_{i}}(\sqcup_{j}B(a))-mn_{i}A.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S10.p10.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="S10.p10.5.1" class="ltx_text">Using Theorem <a href="#Thmintrothm4" title="Theorem D (Subleading asymptotics ECH). ‣ 1.4. Subleading asymptotics of symplectic Weyl laws ‣ 1. Introduction ‣ Packing stability and the subleading asymptotics of symplectic Weyl laws" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D</span></a>, we compute</span></p>
<table id="S10.EGx4" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S10.Ex10"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S10.Ex10.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle c_{k_{i}}(\sqcup_{j}B(a))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mo lspace="0em">⊔</mo><mi>j</mi></msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle c_{k_{i}}(\sqcup_{j}B(a))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S10.Ex10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=2\sqrt{Vk_{i}}+O(1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=2\sqrt{Vk_{i}}+O(1)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S10.Ex11"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S10.Ex11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=2\sqrt{V}\sqrt{m(d_{i}-g+1)\left\lfloor\frac{d_{i}^{2}V}{mA^{2}(d_{i}-g+1)}\right\rfloor}+O(1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mi>V</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>⌊</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mi>d</mi><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>⌋</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=2\sqrt{V}\sqrt{m(d_{i}-g+1)\left\lfloor\frac{d_{i}^{2}V}{mA^{2}(d_{i}-g+1)}\right\rfloor}+O(1)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S10.Ex12"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S10.Ex12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=2\sqrt{V}\sqrt{\frac{d_{i}^{2}V}{A^{2}}+O(d_{i})}+O(1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mi>V</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mi>d</mi><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=2\sqrt{V}\sqrt{\frac{d_{i}^{2}V}{A^{2}}+O(d_{i})}+O(1)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S10.Ex13"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S10.Ex13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=2A^{-1}Vd_{i}\sqrt{1+O(d_{i}^{-1})}+O(1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>d</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=2A^{-1}Vd_{i}\sqrt{1+O(d_{i}^{-1})}+O(1)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S10.Ex14"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S10.Ex14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=2A^{-1}Vd_{i}+O(1)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=2A^{-1}Vd_{i}+O(1).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S10.p10.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="S10.p10.6.1" class="ltx_text">Moreover, we compute</span></p>
<table id="S10.EGx5" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S10.Ex15"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S10.Ex15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle mn_{i}A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle mn_{i}A</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S10.Ex15.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=mA\left\lfloor\frac{d_{i}^{2}V}{mA^{2}(d_{i}-g+1)}\right\rfloor" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>⌊</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mi>d</mi><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>⌋</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=mA\left\lfloor\frac{d_{i}^{2}V}{mA^{2}(d_{i}-g+1)}\right\rfloor</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S10.Ex16"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S10.Ex16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=A^{-1}Vd_{i}\frac{d_{i}}{d_{i}-g+1}+O(1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=A^{-1}Vd_{i}\frac{d_{i}}{d_{i}-g+1}+O(1)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S10.Ex17"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S10.Ex17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=A^{-1}Vd_{i}+O(1)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=A^{-1}Vd_{i}+O(1).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S10.p10.7" class="ltx_p"><span id="S10.p10.7.1" class="ltx_text">Combining these two computations with inequality (<a href="#S10.E8" title="In Proof of Theorem . ‣ 10. Bounding the subleading asymptotics ‣ Packing stability and the subleading asymptotics of symplectic Weyl laws" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10.8</span></a>) yields the desired inequality (<a href="#S10.E6" title="In Proof of Theorem . ‣ 10. Bounding the subleading asymptotics ‣ Packing stability and the subleading asymptotics of symplectic Weyl laws" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10.6</span></a>).
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S10.4" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof of Theorem <a href="#Thmintrothm6" title="Theorem F (Subleading asymptotics link spectral invariants). ‣ 1.4. Subleading asymptotics of symplectic Weyl laws ‣ 1. Introduction ‣ Packing stability and the subleading asymptotics of symplectic Weyl laws" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">F</span></a>.</h6>
<div id="S10.p11" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S10.p11.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S10.p11.1.1" class="ltx_text">We begin by observing that it suffices to establish the inequality</span></p>
<table id="S10.E9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(10.9)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S10.E9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{\underline{L}_{d}}(H)\leq A^{-1}\int_{[0,1]\times\Sigma}Hdt\wedge\omega+O(d^{-1})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><msub><munder accentunder="true"><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><mi>d</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>∧</mo><mi>ω</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{\underline{L}_{d}}(H)\leq A^{-1}\int_{[0,1]\times\Sigma}Hdt\wedge\omega+O(d^{-1})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S10.p11.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S10.p11.2.1" class="ltx_text">for every Hamiltonian <math id="S10.p11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H\in C^{\infty}([0,1]\times\Sigma)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msup><mi>C</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H\in C^{\infty}([0,1]\times\Sigma)</annotation></semantics></math>. Indeed, substituting <math id="S10.p11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{H}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{H}</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="S10.p11.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H</annotation></semantics></math> in inequality (<a href="#S10.E9" title="In Proof of Theorem . ‣ 10. Bounding the subleading asymptotics ‣ Packing stability and the subleading asymptotics of symplectic Weyl laws" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10.9</span></a>) yields</span></p>
<table id="S10.E10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(10.10)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S10.E10.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="c_{\underline{L}_{d}}(\overline{H})\leq A^{-1}\int_{[0,1]\times\Sigma}\overline{H}dt\wedge\omega+O(d^{-1})=-A^{-1}\int_{[0,1]\times\Sigma}Hdt\wedge\omega+O(d^{-1})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><msub><munder accentunder="true"><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><mi>d</mi></msub></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><msub><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi></mrow></msub><mover accent="true"><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mi>d</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>∧</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>O</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><msub><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi></mrow></msub><mi>H</mi><mi>d</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>∧</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>O</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{\underline{L}_{d}}(\overline{H})\leq A^{-1}\int_{[0,1]\times\Sigma}\overline{H}dt\wedge\omega+O(d^{-1})=-A^{-1}\int_{[0,1]\times\Sigma}Hdt\wedge\omega+O(d^{-1}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S10.p11.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S10.p11.3.1" class="ltx_text">By the subadditivity property in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bibx33" title="" class="ltx_ref">CHMSS22</a>, Theorem 1.13]</cite>, we have</span></p>
<table id="S10.E11" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(10.11)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S10.E11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0=c_{\underline{L}_{d}}(0)=c_{\underline{L}_{d}}(H\#\overline{H})\leq c_{\underline{L}_{d}}(H)+c_{\underline{L}_{d}}(\overline{H})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><msub><munder accentunder="true"><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><mi>d</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><msub><munder accentunder="true"><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><mi>d</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>#</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><msub><munder accentunder="true"><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><mi>d</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><msub><munder accentunder="true"><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><mi>d</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0=c_{\underline{L}_{d}}(0)=c_{\underline{L}_{d}}(H\#\overline{H})\leq c_{\underline{L}_{d}}(H)+c_{\underline{L}_{d}}(\overline{H}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S10.p11.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="S10.p11.4.1" class="ltx_text">Combining inequalities (<a href="#S10.E10" title="In Proof of Theorem . ‣ 10. Bounding the subleading asymptotics ‣ Packing stability and the subleading asymptotics of symplectic Weyl laws" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10.10</span></a>) and (<a href="#S10.E11" title="In Proof of Theorem . ‣ 10. Bounding the subleading asymptotics ‣ Packing stability and the subleading asymptotics of symplectic Weyl laws" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10.11</span></a>) yields the desired reverse inequality</span></p>
<table id="S10.Ex18" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S10.Ex18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{\underline{L}_{d}}(H)\geq A^{-1}\int_{[0,1]\times\Sigma}Hdt\wedge\omega+O(d^{-1})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><msub><munder accentunder="true"><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><mi>d</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>∧</mo><mi>ω</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{\underline{L}_{d}}(H)\geq A^{-1}\int_{[0,1]\times\Sigma}Hdt\wedge\omega+O(d^{-1}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S10.p12" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S10.p12.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S10.p12.1.1" class="ltx_text">It remains to prove inequality (<a href="#S10.E9" title="In Proof of Theorem . ‣ 10. Bounding the subleading asymptotics ‣ Packing stability and the subleading asymptotics of symplectic Weyl laws" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10.9</span></a>). This involves the relationship between PFH and link spectral invariants established by Chen <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bibx20" title="" class="ltx_ref">Chea</a>, <a href="#bib.bibx21" title="" class="ltx_ref">Cheb</a>]</cite>. He considers PFH spectral invariants <math id="S10.p12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{\sigma}(\phi,\gamma,H)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>σ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{\sigma}(\phi,\gamma,H)</annotation></semantics></math> in the special case <math id="S10.p12.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi=\operatorname{id}_{\Sigma}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>id</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi=\operatorname{id}_{\Sigma}</annotation></semantics></math>. In this case, the mapping torus <math id="S10.p12.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y_{\phi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y_{\phi}</annotation></semantics></math> is simply given by the product <math id="S10.p12.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{T}\times\Sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝕋</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{T}\times\Sigma</annotation></semantics></math>. For every degree <math id="S10.p12.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, Chen considers the special reference cycle <math id="S10.p12.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma_{d}\coloneqq d\cdot(\mathbb{T}\times\left\{*\right\})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝕋</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∗</mo><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma_{d}\coloneqq d\cdot(\mathbb{T}\times\left\{*\right\})</annotation></semantics></math> for some point <math id="S10.p12.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="*\in\Sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∗</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">*\in\Sigma</annotation></semantics></math>. He constructs a distinguished non-zero PFH class <math id="S10.p12.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e_{d}\in HP(\operatorname{id}_{\Sigma},\gamma_{d})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>id</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e_{d}\in HP(\operatorname{id}_{\Sigma},\gamma_{d})</annotation></semantics></math> called the “PHF unit” and shows the inequality</span></p>
<table id="S10.E12" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(10.12)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S10.E12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="dc_{\underline{L}_{d}}(H)\leq c_{e_{d}}(\operatorname{id}_{\Sigma},\gamma_{d},H)+\int_{\gamma_{d}}Hdt." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><msub><munder accentunder="true"><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><mi>d</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>id</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∫</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></msub><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">dc_{\underline{L}_{d}}(H)\leq c_{e_{d}}(\operatorname{id}_{\Sigma},\gamma_{d},H)+\int_{\gamma_{d}}Hdt.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S10.p12.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S10.p12.2.1" class="ltx_text">Here we follow the notational conventions for link and PFH spectral invariants from <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bibx33" title="" class="ltx_ref">CHMSS22</a>]</cite> and <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bibx45" title="" class="ltx_ref">EH</a>]</cite>, which differ from Chen’s conventions. In particular, Chen absorbs the factor <math id="S10.p12.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math> into the link spectral invariant <math id="S10.p12.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{\underline{L}_{d}}(H)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><msub><munder accentunder="true"><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><mi>d</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{\underline{L}_{d}}(H)</annotation></semantics></math>. By Theorem <a href="#Thmintrothm5" title="Theorem E (Subleading asymptotics PFH). ‣ 1.4. Subleading asymptotics of symplectic Weyl laws ‣ 1. Introduction ‣ Packing stability and the subleading asymptotics of symplectic Weyl laws" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">E</span></a>, we have</span></p>
<table id="S10.E13" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(10.13)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S10.E13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{e_{d}}(\operatorname{id}_{\Sigma},\gamma_{d},H)-c_{e_{d}}(\operatorname{id}_{\Sigma},\gamma_{d},0)+\int_{\gamma_{d}}Hdt=dA^{-1}\int_{[0,1]\times\Sigma}Hdt\wedge\omega+O(1)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>id</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>id</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∫</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></msub><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>∧</mo><mi>ω</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{e_{d}}(\operatorname{id}_{\Sigma},\gamma_{d},H)-c_{e_{d}}(\operatorname{id}_{\Sigma},\gamma_{d},0)+\int_{\gamma_{d}}Hdt=dA^{-1}\int_{[0,1]\times\Sigma}Hdt\wedge\omega+O(1).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S10.p12.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S10.p12.3.1" class="ltx_text">It can be seen from the description given in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bibx20" title="" class="ltx_ref">Chea</a>, <a href="#bib.bibx21" title="" class="ltx_ref">Cheb</a>]</cite> of the class <math id="S10.p12.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e_{d}</annotation></semantics></math> in the PFH chain complex of <math id="S10.p12.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi_{G}^{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>φ</mi><mi>G</mi><mn>1</mn></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi_{G}^{1}</annotation></semantics></math> for a small Morse function <math id="S10.p12.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math> that the spectral invariant <math id="S10.p12.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{e_{d}}(\operatorname{id}_{\Sigma},\gamma_{d},0)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>id</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{e_{d}}(\operatorname{id}_{\Sigma},\gamma_{d},0)</annotation></semantics></math> vanishes. The desired inequality (<a href="#S10.E9" title="In Proof of Theorem . ‣ 10. Bounding the subleading asymptotics ‣ Packing stability and the subleading asymptotics of symplectic Weyl laws" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10.9</span></a>) hence follows from (<a href="#S10.E12" title="In Proof of Theorem . ‣ 10. Bounding the subleading asymptotics ‣ Packing stability and the subleading asymptotics of symplectic Weyl laws" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10.12</span></a>) and (<a href="#S10.E13" title="In Proof of Theorem . ‣ 10. Bounding the subleading asymptotics ‣ Packing stability and the subleading asymptotics of symplectic Weyl laws" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10.13</span></a>).
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S11" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">11. </span><math id="S11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C^{2-\varepsilon}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>C</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C^{2-\varepsilon}</annotation></semantics></math> failure of packing stability</h2>

<div id="S11.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S11.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section we prove Theorem <a href="#Thmintrothm3" title="Theorem C (𝐶^{2-𝜀} failure of packing stability). ‣ 1.3. Limits of packing stability ‣ 1. Introduction ‣ Packing stability and the subleading asymptotics of symplectic Weyl laws" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C</span></a>, i.e. we construct a star-shaped domain <math id="S11.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X\subset\mathbb{R}^{4}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>⊂</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mn>4</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X\subset\mathbb{R}^{4}</annotation></semantics></math> which is <math id="S11.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C^{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C^{1}</annotation></semantics></math> close to the unit ball, whose boundary is <math id="S11.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C^{1,\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>C</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C^{1,\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="S11.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha\in(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\in(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math> and smooth on the complement of a single point, and for which packing stability fails.
<br class="ltx_break"></p>
</div>
<div id="S11.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S11.p2.1" class="ltx_p">We begin by recalling a construction from <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bibx42" title="" class="ltx_ref">Edt24</a>]</cite> which, given a <math id="S11.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math>-periodic Hamiltonian <math id="S11.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H</annotation></semantics></math> on the unit disk <math id="S11.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{D}\subset\mathbb{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔻</mi><mo>⊂</mo><mi>ℂ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{D}\subset\mathbb{C}</annotation></semantics></math>, yields a domain <math id="S11.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X(H)\subset\mathbb{C}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⊂</mo><msup><mi>ℂ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X(H)\subset\mathbb{C}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> such that the characteristic flow on the boundary of <math id="S11.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X(H)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X(H)</annotation></semantics></math> lifts the Hamiltonian flow on <math id="S11.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝔻</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{D}</annotation></semantics></math> induced by <math id="S11.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H</annotation></semantics></math>. It will be convenient to follow the exposition in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bibx1" title="" class="ltx_ref">ABE</a>, §1]</cite>. Recall that <math id="S11.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{T}\coloneqq\mathbb{R}/\mathbb{Z}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝕋</mi><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mi>ℝ</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>ℤ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{T}\coloneqq\mathbb{R}/\mathbb{Z}</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the circle. Define the domain</p>
<table id="S11.Ex1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S11.Ex1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U\coloneqq\left\{(s,t,z)\in\mathbb{R}\times\mathbb{T}\times\mathbb{C}\mid s&gt;\pi(|z|^{2}-1)\right\}\subset\mathbb{R}\times\mathbb{T}\times\mathbb{C}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>ℝ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>𝕋</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>ℂ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow><mo>⊂</mo><mrow><mi>ℝ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>𝕋</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>ℂ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U\coloneqq\left\{(s,t,z)\in\mathbb{R}\times\mathbb{T}\times\mathbb{C}\mid s&gt;\pi(|z|^{2}-1)\right\}\subset\mathbb{R}\times\mathbb{T}\times\mathbb{C}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S11.p2.2" class="ltx_p">and consider the diffeomorphism</p>
<table id="S11.Ex2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S11.Ex2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi:U\rightarrow\mathbb{C}^{*}\times\mathbb{C}\qquad\Phi(s,t,z)\coloneqq e^{2\pi it}\left(\sqrt{1+\frac{s}{\pi}-|z|^{2}},z\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ℂ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>ℂ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:2em;" width="2em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≔</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msqrt><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mi>s</mi><mi>π</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></msqrt><mo>,</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi:U\rightarrow\mathbb{C}^{*}\times\mathbb{C}\qquad\Phi(s,t,z)\coloneqq e^{2\pi it}\left(\sqrt{1+\frac{s}{\pi}-|z|^{2}},z\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S11.p2.3" class="ltx_p">We equip <math id="S11.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>U</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U</annotation></semantics></math> with the symplectic form <math id="S11.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="ds\wedge dt+\omega" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo>∧</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>ω</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">ds\wedge dt+\omega</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="S11.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\omega" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ω</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\omega</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the standard area form on <math id="S11.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ℂ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{C}</annotation></semantics></math>. Moreover, we equip <math id="S11.p2.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{C}^{*}\times\mathbb{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>ℂ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>ℂ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{C}^{*}\times\mathbb{C}</annotation></semantics></math> with the restriction of the standard symplectic form <math id="S11.p2.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\omega_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ω</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\omega_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> on <math id="S11.p2.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{C}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℂ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{C}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>. A simple computation shows that <math id="S11.p2.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi</annotation></semantics></math> is a symplectomorphism with respect to these symplectic forms. Note that the image under <math id="S11.p2.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi</annotation></semantics></math> of a set of the form <math id="S11.p2.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left\{(s,t,z)\in U\mid s&lt;s_{0}\right\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi>U</mi></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\{(s,t,z)\in U\mid s&lt;s_{0}\right\}</annotation></semantics></math> is an open ball with the complex line <math id="S11.p2.m19" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\left\{z_{1}=0\right\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>{</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\{z_{1}=0\right\}</annotation></semantics></math> removed. Let <math id="S11.p2.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H:\mathbb{T}\times\mathbb{D}\rightarrow\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝕋</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>𝔻</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H:\mathbb{T}\times\mathbb{D}\rightarrow\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math> be a compactly supported Hamiltonian such that</p>
<table id="S11.Ex3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S11.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H(t,z)&gt;\pi(|z|^{2}-1)\qquad\text{for all $(t,z)\in\mathbb{T}\times\mathbb{D}$.}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:2em;" width="2em"></mspace><mrow><mtext>for all </mtext><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>𝕋</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>𝔻</mi></mrow></mrow><mtext>.</mtext></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H(t,z)&gt;\pi(|z|^{2}-1)\qquad\text{for all $(t,z)\in\mathbb{T}\times\mathbb{D}$.}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S11.p2.4" class="ltx_p">We define</p>
<table id="S11.Ex4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S11.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="U(H)\coloneqq\left\{(s,t,z)\in U\mid z\in\mathbb{D},s&lt;H(t,z)\right\}\subset U" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>U</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi>U</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>𝔻</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>H</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow><mo>⊂</mo><mi>U</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U(H)\coloneqq\left\{(s,t,z)\in U\mid z\in\mathbb{D},s&lt;H(t,z)\right\}\subset U</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S11.p2.5" class="ltx_p">and set</p>
<table id="S11.Ex5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S11.Ex5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X(H)\coloneqq\operatorname{clos}(\Phi(U(H)))\subset\mathbb{C}^{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mi>clos</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⊂</mo><msup><mi>ℂ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X(H)\coloneqq\operatorname{clos}(\Phi(U(H)))\subset\mathbb{C}^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S11.p2.6" class="ltx_p">The volume of <math id="S11.p2.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X(H)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X(H)</annotation></semantics></math> is given by</p>
<table id="S11.E1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(11.1)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S11.E1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{vol}(X(H))=\operatorname{vol}(B^{4}(\pi))+\int_{[0,1]\times\mathbb{D}}Hdt\wedge\omega." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>vol</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>vol</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>B</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>𝔻</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>∧</mo><mi>ω</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{vol}(X(H))=\operatorname{vol}(B^{4}(\pi))+\int_{[0,1]\times\mathbb{D}}Hdt\wedge\omega.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S11.p2.7" class="ltx_p">If the Hamiltonian <math id="S11.p2.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H</annotation></semantics></math> has regularity <math id="S11.p2.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C^{k,\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C^{k,\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math>, then the same is true for the boundary of <math id="S11.p2.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X(H)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X(H)</annotation></semantics></math>. If <math id="S11.p2.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="S11.p2.m26" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C^{k,\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C^{k,\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math> small, then <math id="S11.p2.m27" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X(H)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X(H)</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="S11.p2.m28" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C^{k,\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C^{k,\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math> close to the unit ball in <math id="S11.p2.m29" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{C}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℂ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{C}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>. The desired domain <math id="S11.p2.m30" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X\subset\mathbb{C}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>⊂</mo><msup><mi>ℂ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X\subset\mathbb{C}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> for which packing stability fails will be of the form <math id="S11.p2.m31" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X(H)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X(H)</annotation></semantics></math> for a carefully constructed <math id="S11.p2.m32" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C^{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C^{1}</annotation></semantics></math> small Hamiltonian <math id="S11.p2.m33" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H</annotation></semantics></math> which is <math id="S11.p2.m34" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C^{1,\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>C</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C^{1,\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="S11.p2.m35" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha\in(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\in(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S11.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S11.p3.1" class="ltx_p">We turn to the definition of <math id="S11.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H</annotation></semantics></math>. Fix a positive parameter <math id="S11.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>. For <math id="S11.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\geq 10" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\geq 10</annotation></semantics></math>, consider the annulus <math id="S11.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{A}_{n}\subset\mathbb{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔸</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>⊂</mo><mi>𝔻</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{A}_{n}\subset\mathbb{D}</annotation></semantics></math> with the same center as <math id="S11.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝔻</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{D}</annotation></semantics></math>, inner radius <math id="S11.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{n}^{-}\coloneqq\frac{2}{\ln(n)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo></msubsup><mo>≔</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{n}^{-}\coloneqq\frac{2}{\ln(n)}</annotation></semantics></math>, and outer radius <math id="S11.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{n}^{+}\coloneqq\frac{2}{\ln(n-1)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo>≔</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{n}^{+}\coloneqq\frac{2}{\ln(n-1)}</annotation></semantics></math>. Note that the interiors of the annuli <math id="S11.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{A}_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝔸</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{A}_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> are pairwise disjoint and that the width <math id="S11.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{n}^{+}-R_{n}^{-}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{n}^{+}-R_{n}^{-}</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="S11.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{A}_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝔸</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{A}_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> is strictly bigger than <math id="S11.p3.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{2}{n\ln(n)^{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo>⁡</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{2}{n\ln(n)^{2}}</annotation></semantics></math>. For each <math id="S11.p3.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math>, we choose <math id="S11.p3.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> pairwise disjoint disks <math id="S11.p3.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{n}^{1},\dots,D_{n}^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>D</mi><mi>n</mi><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>D</mi><mi>n</mi><mi>n</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{n}^{1},\dots,D_{n}^{n}</annotation></semantics></math> of radius <math id="S11.p3.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{n}\coloneqq\frac{1}{n\ln(n)^{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>≔</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo>⁡</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{n}\coloneqq\frac{1}{n\ln(n)^{2}}</annotation></semantics></math> inside the interior of <math id="S11.p3.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{A}_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝔸</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{A}_{n}</annotation></semantics></math>. In order to see that this is possible, note that the diameter <math id="S11.p3.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2r_{n}=\frac{2}{n\ln(n)^{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo>⁡</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2r_{n}=\frac{2}{n\ln(n)^{2}}</annotation></semantics></math> of each of the disks <math id="S11.p3.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{n}^{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>D</mi><mi>n</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{n}^{i}</annotation></semantics></math> is strictly smaller than the width of <math id="S11.p3.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{A}_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝔸</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{A}_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> and the sum of the diameters of the <math id="S11.p3.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> disks <math id="S11.p3.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{n}^{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>D</mi><mi>n</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{n}^{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, which is given by <math id="S11.p3.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2r_{n}n=\frac{2}{\ln(n)^{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo>⁡</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2r_{n}n=\frac{2}{\ln(n)^{2}}</annotation></semantics></math>, is strictly smaller than the circumference of the inner boundary circle of <math id="S11.p3.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{A}_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝔸</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{A}_{n}</annotation></semantics></math>, which is given by <math id="S11.p3.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2\pi R_{n}^{-}=\frac{4\pi}{\ln(n)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2\pi R_{n}^{-}=\frac{4\pi}{\ln(n)}</annotation></semantics></math>. For <math id="S11.p3.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, let <math id="S11.p3.m26" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{D}_{r}\subset\mathbb{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔻</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>⊂</mo><mi>ℂ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{D}_{r}\subset\mathbb{C}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the disk of radius <math id="S11.p3.m27" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math> centered at the origin. Fix a smooth radially symmetric function <math id="S11.p3.m28" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f:\mathbb{D}\rightarrow\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>𝔻</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f:\mathbb{D}\rightarrow\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math> which is non-increasing in the radial direction, satisfies <math id="S11.p3.m29" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(0)=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(0)=1</annotation></semantics></math>, and is supported inside <math id="S11.p3.m30" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{D}_{\frac{1}{10}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝔻</mi><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>10</mn></mfrac></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{D}_{\frac{1}{10}}</annotation></semantics></math>. For each <math id="S11.p3.m31" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math>, we set</p>
<table id="S11.Ex6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S11.Ex6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{n}:\mathbb{D}_{r_{n}}\rightarrow\mathbb{R}\qquad f_{n}(z)\coloneqq\frac{\ln(n)}{n^{2}}f(\frac{z}{r_{n}})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔻</mi><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:2em;" width="2em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mfrac><mi>z</mi><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{n}:\mathbb{D}_{r_{n}}\rightarrow\mathbb{R}\qquad f_{n}(z)\coloneqq\frac{\ln(n)}{n^{2}}f(\frac{z}{r_{n}}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S11.p3.2" class="ltx_p">For <math id="S11.p3.m32" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1\leq i\leq n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1\leq i\leq n</annotation></semantics></math>, let <math id="S11.p3.m33" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{n}^{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mi>n</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{n}^{i}</annotation></semantics></math> be the function obtained by pushing <math id="S11.p3.m34" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> forward via the translation moving <math id="S11.p3.m35" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{D}_{r_{n}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝔻</mi><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{D}_{r_{n}}</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S11.p3.m36" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{n}^{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>D</mi><mi>n</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{n}^{i}</annotation></semantics></math>. Fix a compactly supported smooth function <math id="S11.p3.m37" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g:(-\frac{1}{2},\frac{1}{2})\rightarrow[0,\infty)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g:(-\frac{1}{2},\frac{1}{2})\rightarrow[0,\infty)</annotation></semantics></math> with integral <math id="S11.p3.m38" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\int g(t)dt=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\int g(t)dt=1</annotation></semantics></math> and set</p>
<table id="S11.Ex7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S11.Ex7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{n}(t)\coloneqq\ln(n)g(\ln(n)t)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{n}(t)\coloneqq\ln(n)g(\ln(n)t).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S11.p3.3" class="ltx_p">Note that the support of <math id="S11.p3.m39" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> is contained in <math id="S11.p3.m40" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(-\frac{1}{2\ln(n)},\frac{1}{2\ln(n)})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(-\frac{1}{2\ln(n)},\frac{1}{2\ln(n)})</annotation></semantics></math> and that we have <math id="S11.p3.m41" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\int g_{n}(t)dt=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>∫</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\int g_{n}(t)dt=1</annotation></semantics></math>. We regard each <math id="S11.p3.m42" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> as a function <math id="S11.p3.m43" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{n}:\mathbb{T}\rightarrow[0,\infty)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>𝕋</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{n}:\mathbb{T}\rightarrow[0,\infty)</annotation></semantics></math>. Now define</p>
<table id="S11.Ex8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S11.Ex8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{k}:\mathbb{T}\times\mathbb{D}\rightarrow\mathbb{R}\qquad H_{k}(t,z)\coloneqq\lambda\sum\limits_{n=10}^{k}g_{n}(t)\sum\limits_{i=1}^{n}f_{n}^{i}(z)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝕋</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>𝔻</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:2em;" width="2em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow><mi>k</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><mrow><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mi>n</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{k}:\mathbb{T}\times\mathbb{D}\rightarrow\mathbb{R}\qquad H_{k}(t,z)\coloneqq\lambda\sum\limits_{n=10}^{k}g_{n}(t)\sum\limits_{i=1}^{n}f_{n}^{i}(z)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S11.p3.4" class="ltx_p">and</p>
<table id="S11.Ex9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S11.Ex9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H:\mathbb{T}\times\mathbb{D}\rightarrow\mathbb{R}\qquad H(t,z)\coloneqq\lim_{k\rightarrow\infty}H_{k}(t,z)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝕋</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>𝔻</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:2em;" width="2em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">≔</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">lim</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H:\mathbb{T}\times\mathbb{D}\rightarrow\mathbb{R}\qquad H(t,z)\coloneqq\lim_{k\rightarrow\infty}H_{k}(t,z).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S11.p3.5" class="ltx_p">The limit is uniform, implying that <math id="S11.p3.m44" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H</annotation></semantics></math> is continuous. Each compact subset of <math id="S11.p3.m45" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{T}\times\mathbb{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝕋</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>𝔻</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{T}\times\mathbb{D}</annotation></semantics></math> which does not contain the point <math id="S11.p3.m46" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(0,0)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(0,0)</annotation></semantics></math> intersects the support of <math id="S11.p3.m47" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{n}(t)f_{n}^{i}(z)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mi>n</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{n}(t)f_{n}^{i}(z)</annotation></semantics></math> for only finitely many values of <math id="S11.p3.m48" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus <math id="S11.p3.m49" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H</annotation></semantics></math> is smooth on the complement of the point <math id="S11.p3.m50" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(0,0)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(0,0)</annotation></semantics></math>. The sequence of Hamiltonian isotopies <math id="S11.p3.m51" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\varphi_{H_{k}}^{t})_{t\in[0,1]}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>φ</mi><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\varphi_{H_{k}}^{t})_{t\in[0,1]}</annotation></semantics></math> converges in the <math id="S11.p3.m52" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C^{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>C</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C^{0}</annotation></semantics></math> topology to an isotopy in <math id="S11.p3.m53" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{Homeo}_{c}(\mathbb{D},\omega)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Homeo</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝔻</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{Homeo}_{c}(\mathbb{D},\omega)</annotation></semantics></math>, the space of compactly supported area preserving homeomorphisms of <math id="S11.p3.m54" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝔻</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{D}</annotation></semantics></math>. We abbreviate this isotopy by <math id="S11.p3.m55" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\varphi_{H}^{t})_{t\in[0,1]}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>φ</mi><mi>H</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\varphi_{H}^{t})_{t\in[0,1]}</annotation></semantics></math>. By definition, this means that <math id="S11.p3.m56" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi_{H}^{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>φ</mi><mi>H</mi><mn>1</mn></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi_{H}^{1}</annotation></semantics></math> is contained in the group of hameomorphisms <math id="S11.p3.m57" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{Hameo}_{c}(\mathbb{D},\omega)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Hameo</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝔻</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{Hameo}_{c}(\mathbb{D},\omega)</annotation></semantics></math>. This group was introduced by Oh an Müller in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bibx73" title="" class="ltx_ref">OM07</a>]</cite>, see also <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bibx34" title="" class="ltx_ref">CHMSS</a>, Definition 2.2]</cite>. It will also be convenient to have an autonomous Hamiltonian <math id="S11.p3.m58" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{H}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>H</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{H}</annotation></semantics></math> generating the same hameomorphism <math id="S11.p3.m59" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi_{H}^{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>φ</mi><mi>H</mi><mn>1</mn></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi_{H}^{1}</annotation></semantics></math>. We set</p>
<table id="S11.Ex10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S11.Ex10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{H}_{k}:\mathbb{D}\rightarrow\mathbb{R}\qquad\tilde{H}_{k}(z)\coloneqq\lambda\sum\limits_{n=10}^{k}\sum\limits_{i=1}^{n}f_{n}^{i}(z)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>H</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>𝔻</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:2em;" width="2em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>H</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow><mi>k</mi></munderover><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><mrow><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mi>n</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{H}_{k}:\mathbb{D}\rightarrow\mathbb{R}\qquad\tilde{H}_{k}(z)\coloneqq\lambda\sum\limits_{n=10}^{k}\sum\limits_{i=1}^{n}f_{n}^{i}(z)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S11.p3.6" class="ltx_p">and</p>
<table id="S11.Ex11" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S11.Ex11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{H}:\mathbb{D}\rightarrow\mathbb{R}\qquad\tilde{H}(z)\coloneqq\lim_{k\rightarrow\infty}\tilde{H}_{k}(z)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>H</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>𝔻</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:2em;" width="2em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>H</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">≔</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">lim</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>H</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{H}:\mathbb{D}\rightarrow\mathbb{R}\qquad\tilde{H}(z)\coloneqq\lim_{k\rightarrow\infty}\tilde{H}_{k}(z).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S11.p3.7" class="ltx_p">Then the Hamiltonian isotopies <math id="S11.p3.m60" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\varphi_{\tilde{H}_{k}}^{t})_{t\in[0,1]}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>φ</mi><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>H</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\varphi_{\tilde{H}_{k}}^{t})_{t\in[0,1]}</annotation></semantics></math> converge in the <math id="S11.p3.m61" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C^{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>C</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C^{0}</annotation></semantics></math> topology to an isotopy <math id="S11.p3.m62" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\varphi_{\tilde{H}}^{t})_{t\in[0,1]}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>φ</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>H</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\varphi_{\tilde{H}}^{t})_{t\in[0,1]}</annotation></semantics></math> in <math id="S11.p3.m63" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{Homeo}_{c}(\mathbb{D},\omega)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Homeo</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝔻</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{Homeo}_{c}(\mathbb{D},\omega)</annotation></semantics></math>. Since <math id="S11.p3.m64" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi_{H_{k}}^{1}=\varphi_{\tilde{H}_{k}}^{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>φ</mi><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>φ</mi><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>H</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub><mn>1</mn></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi_{H_{k}}^{1}=\varphi_{\tilde{H}_{k}}^{1}</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="S11.p3.m65" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>, we have <math id="S11.p3.m66" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi_{H}^{1}=\varphi_{\tilde{H}}^{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>φ</mi><mi>H</mi><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>φ</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>H</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi_{H}^{1}=\varphi_{\tilde{H}}^{1}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S11.Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S11.Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 11.1</span></span><span id="S11.Thmtheorem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S11.Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S11.Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S11.Thmtheorem1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The Hamiltonians <math id="S11.Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S11.Thmtheorem1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{H}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>H</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{H}</annotation></semantics></math> are contained in the Hölder space <math id="S11.Thmtheorem1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C^{1,\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>C</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C^{1,\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math> for every <math id="S11.Thmtheorem1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha\in(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\in(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math>, but not in <math id="S11.Thmtheorem1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C^{1,1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>C</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C^{1,1}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S11.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S11.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S11.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S11.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">For <math id="S11.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\neq y\in\mathbb{D}_{r_{n}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>𝔻</mi><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\neq y\in\mathbb{D}_{r_{n}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S11.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha\in(0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\in(0,1]</annotation></semantics></math>, we compute</span></p>
<table id="S11.EGx6" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S11.Ex12"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S11.Ex12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{|df_{n}(x)-df_{n}(y)|}{|x-y|^{\alpha}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mi>α</mi></msup></mfrac></mstyle><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{|df_{n}(x)-df_{n}(y)|}{|x-y|^{\alpha}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S11.Ex12.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{\ln(n)}{n^{2}}\cdot\frac{|\frac{1}{r_{n}}df(\frac{x}{r_{n}})-\frac{1}{r_{n}}df(\frac{y}{r_{n}})|}{r_{n}^{\alpha}|\frac{x}{r_{n}}-\frac{y}{r_{n}}|^{\alpha}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mfrac><mi>x</mi><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mfrac><mi>y</mi><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>n</mi><mi>α</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>x</mi><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mi>y</mi><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mfrac></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mi>α</mi></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{\ln(n)}{n^{2}}\cdot\frac{|\frac{1}{r_{n}}df(\frac{x}{r_{n}})-\frac{1}{r_{n}}df(\frac{y}{r_{n}})|}{r_{n}^{\alpha}|\frac{x}{r_{n}}-\frac{y}{r_{n}}|^{\alpha}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S11.Ex13"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S11.Ex13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=n^{\alpha-1}\ln(n)^{3+2\alpha}\frac{|df(\frac{x}{r_{n}})-df(\frac{y}{r_{n}})|}{|\frac{x}{r_{n}}-\frac{y}{r_{n}}|^{\alpha}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>n</mi><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo>⁡</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mfrac><mi>x</mi><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mfrac><mi>y</mi><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>x</mi><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mi>y</mi><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mfrac></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mi>α</mi></msup></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=n^{\alpha-1}\ln(n)^{3+2\alpha}\frac{|df(\frac{x}{r_{n}})-df(\frac{y}{r_{n}})|}{|\frac{x}{r_{n}}-\frac{y}{r_{n}}|^{\alpha}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S11.p4.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S11.p4.2.1" class="ltx_text">This implies that</span></p>
<table id="S11.Ex14" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S11.Ex14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[df_{n}]_{C^{0,\alpha}}=n^{\alpha-1}\ln(n)^{3+2\alpha}[df]_{C^{0,\alpha}}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><msup><mi>C</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msup></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>n</mi><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo>⁡</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><msup><mi>C</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msup></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[df_{n}]_{C^{0,\alpha}}=n^{\alpha-1}\ln(n)^{3+2\alpha}[df]_{C^{0,\alpha}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S11.p4.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S11.p4.3.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="S11.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[\cdot]_{C^{0,\alpha}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><msup><mi>C</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msup></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[\cdot]_{C^{0,\alpha}}</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the <math id="S11.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C^{0,\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>C</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C^{0,\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math> seminorm. If <math id="S11.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha\in(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\in(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="S11.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n^{\alpha-1}\ln(n)^{3+2\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>n</mi><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo>⁡</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n^{\alpha-1}\ln(n)^{3+2\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math> converges to zero as <math id="S11.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> tends to infinity. Using this, we see that <math id="S11.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{H}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>H</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{H}</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="S11.p4.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C^{1,\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>C</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C^{1,\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="S11.p4.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha&lt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha&lt;1</annotation></semantics></math>. If <math id="S11.p4.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha=1</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="S11.p4.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n^{\alpha-1}\ln(n)^{3+2\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>n</mi><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo>⁡</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n^{\alpha-1}\ln(n)^{3+2\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math> diverges, which implies that <math id="S11.p4.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{H}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>H</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{H}</annotation></semantics></math> is not <math id="S11.p4.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C^{1,1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>C</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C^{1,1}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S11.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S11.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S11.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">The proof that <math id="S11.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H</annotation></semantics></math> is in <math id="S11.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C^{1,\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>C</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C^{1,\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="S11.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha&lt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha&lt;1</annotation></semantics></math> but not for <math id="S11.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha=1</annotation></semantics></math> is similar. A short computation shows that <math id="S11.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[dg_{n}]_{C^{0,\alpha}}=\ln(n)^{2+\alpha}[dg]_{C^{0,\alpha}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><msup><mi>C</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msup></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><msup><mi>C</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msup></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[dg_{n}]_{C^{0,\alpha}}=\ln(n)^{2+\alpha}[dg]_{C^{0,\alpha}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Since logarithmic terms are dominated by negative powers of <math id="S11.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math>, we see that <math id="S11.p5.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[d(g_{n}f_{n})]_{C^{0,\alpha}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><msup><mi>C</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msup></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[d(g_{n}f_{n})]_{C^{0,\alpha}}</annotation></semantics></math> converges to zero for <math id="S11.p5.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha&lt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha&lt;1</annotation></semantics></math> and diverges for <math id="S11.p5.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha=1</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S11.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S11.p6.1" class="ltx_p">Lemma <a href="#S11.Thmtheorem1" title="Lemma 11.1. ‣ 11. 𝐶^{2-𝜀} failure of packing stability ‣ Packing stability and the subleading asymptotics of symplectic Weyl laws" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">11.1</span></a> implies that the domain <math id="S11.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X(H)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X(H)</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="S11.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C^{1,\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>C</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C^{1,\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="S11.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha&lt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha&lt;1</annotation></semantics></math>, but not <math id="S11.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C^{1,1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>C</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C^{1,1}</annotation></semantics></math>. Since <math id="S11.p6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H</annotation></semantics></math> is smooth on the complement of a single point, the same is true for the domain <math id="S11.p6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X(H)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X(H)</annotation></semantics></math>. By choosing the parameter <math id="S11.p6.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> small, we can make sure that <math id="S11.p6.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X(H)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X(H)</annotation></semantics></math> is arbitrarily <math id="S11.p6.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C^{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C^{1}</annotation></semantics></math> close to the unit ball in <math id="S11.p6.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{C}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℂ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{C}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>. Our goal is to show that the error terms in the Weyl law for the alternative ECH capacities (see Remark <a href="#S1.Thmtheorem2" title="Remark 1.2. ‣ 1.4. Subleading asymptotics of symplectic Weyl laws ‣ 1. Introduction ‣ Packing stability and the subleading asymptotics of symplectic Weyl laws" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1.2</span></a>) of <math id="S11.p6.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X(H)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X(H)</annotation></semantics></math> diverge to <math id="S11.p6.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-\infty</annotation></semantics></math>. More precisely, let us write</p>
<table id="S11.Ex15" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S11.Ex15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{k}^{\operatorname{alt}}(X(H))=2\sqrt{\operatorname{vol}(X(H))k}+e_{k}^{\operatorname{alt}}(X(H))." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>alt</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mrow><mi>vol</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>e</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>alt</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{k}^{\operatorname{alt}}(X(H))=2\sqrt{\operatorname{vol}(X(H))k}+e_{k}^{\operatorname{alt}}(X(H)).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S11.p6.2" class="ltx_p">We will show:</p>
</div>
<div id="S11.Thmtheorem2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proposition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S11.Thmtheorem2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition 11.2</span></span><span id="S11.Thmtheorem2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S11.Thmtheorem2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S11.Thmtheorem2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S11.Thmtheorem2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">We have <math id="S11.Thmtheorem2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lim_{k\rightarrow\infty}e_{k}^{\operatorname{alt}}(X(H))=-\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>lim</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><msubsup><mi>e</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>alt</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lim_{k\rightarrow\infty}e_{k}^{\operatorname{alt}}(X(H))=-\infty</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S11.Thmtheorem3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_remark">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S11.Thmtheorem3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Remark 11.3</span></span><span id="S11.Thmtheorem3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S11.Thmtheorem3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S11.Thmtheorem3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">It should also be the case that the error terms in the Weyl law for the usual ECH capacities of <math id="S11.Thmtheorem3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X(H)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X(H)</annotation></semantics></math> diverge to <math id="S11.Thmtheorem3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-\infty</annotation></semantics></math>. The reason we formulate Proposition <a href="#S11.Thmtheorem2" title="Proposition 11.2. ‣ 11. 𝐶^{2-𝜀} failure of packing stability ‣ Packing stability and the subleading asymptotics of symplectic Weyl laws" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">11.2</span></a> for the alternative ECH capacities instead of the original ones is that we rely on certain inequalities between PFH spectral invariants and capacities from <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bibx45" title="" class="ltx_ref">EH</a>]</cite>. These inequalities are stated for the alternative ECH capacities, but also expected to hold for the usual ones.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S11.Thmtheorem4" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_remark">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S11.Thmtheorem4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Remark 11.4</span></span><span id="S11.Thmtheorem4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S11.Thmtheorem4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S11.Thmtheorem4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The domain <math id="S11.Thmtheorem4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X(H)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X(H)</annotation></semantics></math> is the limit of smooth domains <math id="S11.Thmtheorem4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X(H_{k})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X(H_{k})</annotation></semantics></math>. A direct computation shows that the Ruelle invariants <math id="S11.Thmtheorem4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{Ru}(X(H_{k}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Ru</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{Ru}(X(H_{k}))</annotation></semantics></math> of these domains diverge to <math id="S11.Thmtheorem4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="+\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">+\infty</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore, Proposition <a href="#S11.Thmtheorem2" title="Proposition 11.2. ‣ 11. 𝐶^{2-𝜀} failure of packing stability ‣ Packing stability and the subleading asymptotics of symplectic Weyl laws" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">11.2</span></a> is expected in view of Hutchings’ conjecture, see equation (<a href="#S1.E3" title="In 1.4. Subleading asymptotics of symplectic Weyl laws ‣ 1. Introduction ‣ Packing stability and the subleading asymptotics of symplectic Weyl laws" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1.3</span></a>).</p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S11.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S11.p7.1" class="ltx_p">Theorem <a href="#Thmintrothm3" title="Theorem C (𝐶^{2-𝜀} failure of packing stability). ‣ 1.3. Limits of packing stability ‣ 1. Introduction ‣ Packing stability and the subleading asymptotics of symplectic Weyl laws" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C</span></a> is an easy consequence of Theorem <a href="#Thmintrothm4" title="Theorem D (Subleading asymptotics ECH). ‣ 1.4. Subleading asymptotics of symplectic Weyl laws ‣ 1. Introduction ‣ Packing stability and the subleading asymptotics of symplectic Weyl laws" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D</span></a>, Remark <a href="#S1.Thmtheorem2" title="Remark 1.2. ‣ 1.4. Subleading asymptotics of symplectic Weyl laws ‣ 1. Introduction ‣ Packing stability and the subleading asymptotics of symplectic Weyl laws" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1.2</span></a>, and Proposition <a href="#S11.Thmtheorem2" title="Proposition 11.2. ‣ 11. 𝐶^{2-𝜀} failure of packing stability ‣ Packing stability and the subleading asymptotics of symplectic Weyl laws" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">11.2</span></a>. Indeed, let <math id="S11.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W\subset\mathbb{R}^{4}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo>⊂</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mn>4</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W\subset\mathbb{R}^{4}</annotation></semantics></math> be a compact domain with smooth boundary and assume by contradiction that <math id="S11.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p^{W}(X(H))=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>p</mi><mi>W</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p^{W}(X(H))=1</annotation></semantics></math>. After rescaling, we can assume that <math id="S11.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>W</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W</annotation></semantics></math> has the same volume as <math id="S11.p7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X(H)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X(H)</annotation></semantics></math>. The identity <math id="S11.p7.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p^{W}(X(H))=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>p</mi><mi>W</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p^{W}(X(H))=1</annotation></semantics></math> then implies that <math id="S11.p7.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="rW" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>W</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">rW</annotation></semantics></math> admits a symplectic embedding into <math id="S11.p7.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X(H)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X(H)</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="S11.p7.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r\in(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r\in(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math>. By monotonicity of capacities, we obtain <math id="S11.p7.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{k}^{\operatorname{alt}}(W)\leq c_{k}^{\operatorname{alt}}(X(H))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>alt</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>alt</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{k}^{\operatorname{alt}}(W)\leq c_{k}^{\operatorname{alt}}(X(H))</annotation></semantics></math>. Since <math id="S11.p7.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{vol}(W)=\operatorname{vol}(X(H))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>vol</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>vol</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{vol}(W)=\operatorname{vol}(X(H))</annotation></semantics></math>, we deduce that <math id="S11.p7.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e_{k}^{\operatorname{alt}}(W)\leq e_{k}^{\operatorname{alt}}(X(H))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>e</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>alt</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>e</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>alt</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e_{k}^{\operatorname{alt}}(W)\leq e_{k}^{\operatorname{alt}}(X(H))</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="S11.p7.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>. But <math id="S11.p7.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e_{k}^{\operatorname{alt}}(W)=O(1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>e</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>alt</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e_{k}^{\operatorname{alt}}(W)=O(1)</annotation></semantics></math> by Theorem <a href="#Thmintrothm4" title="Theorem D (Subleading asymptotics ECH). ‣ 1.4. Subleading asymptotics of symplectic Weyl laws ‣ 1. Introduction ‣ Packing stability and the subleading asymptotics of symplectic Weyl laws" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D</span></a> and Remark <a href="#S1.Thmtheorem2" title="Remark 1.2. ‣ 1.4. Subleading asymptotics of symplectic Weyl laws ‣ 1. Introduction ‣ Packing stability and the subleading asymptotics of symplectic Weyl laws" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1.2</span></a>, contradicting Proposition <a href="#S11.Thmtheorem2" title="Proposition 11.2. ‣ 11. 𝐶^{2-𝜀} failure of packing stability ‣ Packing stability and the subleading asymptotics of symplectic Weyl laws" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">11.2</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S11.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S11.p8.1" class="ltx_p">It remains to prove Proposition <a href="#S11.Thmtheorem2" title="Proposition 11.2. ‣ 11. 𝐶^{2-𝜀} failure of packing stability ‣ Packing stability and the subleading asymptotics of symplectic Weyl laws" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">11.2</span></a>. We obtain the necessary estimates on the error terms <math id="S11.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e_{k}^{\operatorname{alt}}(X(H))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>e</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>alt</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e_{k}^{\operatorname{alt}}(X(H))</annotation></semantics></math> in a slightly roundabout way which involves both link spectral invariants and PFH spectral invariants. The reason for this detour is that while we do not know how to compute the (alternative) ECH capacities of <math id="S11.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X(H)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X(H)</annotation></semantics></math>, the link spectral invariants of the Hamiltonian <math id="S11.p8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H</annotation></semantics></math> are easy to compute for appropriate choices of links. PFH is used as an intermediary between link spectral invariants and alternative ECH capacities. We make use of the work of Chen <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bibx20" title="" class="ltx_ref">Chea</a>, <a href="#bib.bibx21" title="" class="ltx_ref">Cheb</a>]</cite>, which relates link spectral invariants and PFH spectral invariants. We also rely on methods from <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bibx45" title="" class="ltx_ref">EH</a>]</cite> to relate PFH spectral invariants and alternative ECH capacities.</p>
</div>
<div id="S11.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S11.p9.1" class="ltx_p">We begin by estimating the link spectral invariants of <math id="S11.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="S11.p9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(S^{2},\omega)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(S^{2},\omega)</annotation></semantics></math> be the sphere of area <math id="S11.p9.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A\coloneqq\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>≔</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A\coloneqq\pi</annotation></semantics></math> obtained from <math id="S11.p9.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝔻</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{D}</annotation></semantics></math> by collapsing the boundary circle to a point. Any compactly supported Hamiltonian <math id="S11.p9.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math> on <math id="S11.p9.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝔻</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{D}</annotation></semantics></math> descends to a Hamiltonian on <math id="S11.p9.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>S</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>. In the following, we will use the same letter <math id="S11.p9.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math> for this Hamiltonian. Recall from <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bibx33" title="" class="ltx_ref">CHMSS22</a>]</cite> that a Lagrangian link <math id="S11.p9.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underline{L}\subset S^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><munder accentunder="true"><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><mo>⊂</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underline{L}\subset S^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> is the disjoint union of finitely many smoothly embedded circles. We call a link <math id="S11.p9.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underline{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><munder accentunder="true"><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underline{L}</annotation></semantics></math> monotone if all components of <math id="S11.p9.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S^{2}\setminus\underline{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>S</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>∖</mo><munder accentunder="true"><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S^{2}\setminus\underline{L}</annotation></semantics></math> have equal area. This area must be equal to <math id="S11.p9.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{A}{d+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{A}{d+1}</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="S11.p9.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the number of components of <math id="S11.p9.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underline{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><munder accentunder="true"><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underline{L}</annotation></semantics></math>. Given a monotone link <math id="S11.p9.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underline{L}\subset S^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><munder accentunder="true"><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><mo>⊂</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underline{L}\subset S^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, the paper <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bibx33" title="" class="ltx_ref">CHMSS22</a>]</cite> introduces a spectral invariant</p>
<table id="S11.Ex16" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S11.Ex16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{\underline{L}}:C^{\infty}([0,1]\times S^{2})\rightarrow\mathbb{R}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><munder accentunder="true"><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>C</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{\underline{L}}:C^{\infty}([0,1]\times S^{2})\rightarrow\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S11.p9.2" class="ltx_p">called link spectral invariant. The main properties of link spectral invariants are summarized in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bibx33" title="" class="ltx_ref">CHMSS22</a>, Theorem 1.1 &amp; 1.13]</cite>. By the Hofer Lipschitz property, each <math id="S11.p9.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{\underline{L}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>c</mi><munder accentunder="true"><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{\underline{L}}</annotation></semantics></math> is Lipschitz continuous with respect to the <math id="S11.p9.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C^{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>C</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C^{0}</annotation></semantics></math> norm on <math id="S11.p9.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C^{\infty}([0,1]\times S^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>C</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C^{\infty}([0,1]\times S^{2})</annotation></semantics></math>. This implies that <math id="S11.p9.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{\underline{L}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>c</mi><munder accentunder="true"><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{\underline{L}}</annotation></semantics></math> admits a continuous extension to <math id="S11.p9.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C^{0}([0,1]\times S^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>C</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C^{0}([0,1]\times S^{2})</annotation></semantics></math>. In particular, <math id="S11.p9.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{\underline{L}}(H)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><munder accentunder="true"><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{\underline{L}}(H)</annotation></semantics></math> is defined for every link <math id="S11.p9.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underline{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><munder accentunder="true"><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underline{L}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S11.Thmtheorem5" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S11.Thmtheorem5.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 11.5</span></span><span id="S11.Thmtheorem5.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S11.Thmtheorem5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S11.Thmtheorem5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S11.Thmtheorem5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For each <math id="S11.Thmtheorem5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math>, let <math id="S11.Thmtheorem5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underline{L}_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><munder accentunder="true"><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><mi>d</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underline{L}_{d}</annotation></semantics></math> be a monotone <math id="S11.Thmtheorem5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math>-component link in <math id="S11.Thmtheorem5.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(S^{2},\omega)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(S^{2},\omega)</annotation></semantics></math>. Then</span></p>
<table id="S11.E2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(11.2)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S11.E2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="dc_{\underline{L}_{d}}(H)-dA^{-1}\int_{[0,1]\times S^{2}}Hdt\wedge\omega\rightarrow-\infty\qquad(d\rightarrow+\infty)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><msub><munder accentunder="true"><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><mi>d</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></msub><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>∧</mo><mi>ω</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:2em;" width="2em"></mspace><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">dc_{\underline{L}_{d}}(H)-dA^{-1}\int_{[0,1]\times S^{2}}Hdt\wedge\omega\rightarrow-\infty\qquad(d\rightarrow+\infty).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S11.Thmtheorem6" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_remark">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S11.Thmtheorem6.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Remark 11.6</span></span><span id="S11.Thmtheorem6.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S11.Thmtheorem6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S11.Thmtheorem6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The factor <math id="S11.Thmtheorem6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math> is not present in the Weyl law <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bibx33" title="" class="ltx_ref">CHMSS22</a>, Theorem 1.1]</cite> because there the surface is normalized to have area <math id="S11.Thmtheorem6.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S11.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S11.p10" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S11.p10.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S11.p10.1.1" class="ltx_text">We claim that</span></p>
<table id="S11.E3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(11.3)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S11.E3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|c_{\underline{L}_{d}}(H)-c_{\underline{L}_{d}^{\prime}}(H)|\leq\frac{2A}{d}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><msub><munder accentunder="true"><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><mi>d</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><msubsup><munder accentunder="true"><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><mi>d</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><mi>d</mi></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|c_{\underline{L}_{d}}(H)-c_{\underline{L}_{d}^{\prime}}(H)|\leq\frac{2A}{d}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S11.p10.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S11.p10.2.1" class="ltx_text">for any two monotone <math id="S11.p10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math>-component links <math id="S11.p10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underline{L}_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><munder accentunder="true"><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><mi>d</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underline{L}_{d}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S11.p10.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underline{L}_{d}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><munder accentunder="true"><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><mi>d</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underline{L}_{d}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>. This inequality implies that if (<a href="#S11.E2" title="In Lemma 11.5. ‣ 11. 𝐶^{2-𝜀} failure of packing stability ‣ Packing stability and the subleading asymptotics of symplectic Weyl laws" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">11.2</span></a>) holds for one sequence of monotone links, then it holds for every other sequence of monotone links as well. This means that once we know inequality (<a href="#S11.E3" title="In Proof. ‣ 11. 𝐶^{2-𝜀} failure of packing stability ‣ Packing stability and the subleading asymptotics of symplectic Weyl laws" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">11.3</span></a>), we can reduce ourselves to verifying (<a href="#S11.E2" title="In Lemma 11.5. ‣ 11. 𝐶^{2-𝜀} failure of packing stability ‣ Packing stability and the subleading asymptotics of symplectic Weyl laws" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">11.2</span></a>) for one single carefully constructed sequence of links. We prove inequality (<a href="#S11.E3" title="In Proof. ‣ 11. 𝐶^{2-𝜀} failure of packing stability ‣ Packing stability and the subleading asymptotics of symplectic Weyl laws" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">11.3</span></a>). Let <math id="S11.p10.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underline{L}_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><munder accentunder="true"><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><mi>d</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underline{L}_{d}</annotation></semantics></math> be a monotone <math id="S11.p10.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math>-component link. If <math id="S11.p10.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G\in C^{\infty}_{c}([0,1]\times\mathbb{D})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mi>c</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>𝔻</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G\in C^{\infty}_{c}([0,1]\times\mathbb{D})</annotation></semantics></math> is a smooth Hamiltonian compactly supported in the interior of the disk, then <math id="S11.p10.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{\underline{L}_{d}}(G)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><msub><munder accentunder="true"><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><mi>d</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{\underline{L}_{d}}(G)</annotation></semantics></math> only depends on the time-<math id="S11.p10.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math> map <math id="S11.p10.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi_{G}^{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>φ</mi><mi>G</mi><mn>1</mn></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi_{G}^{1}</annotation></semantics></math> by the homotopy invariance property in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bibx33" title="" class="ltx_ref">CHMSS22</a>, Theorem 1.13]</cite>. The resulting map</span></p>
<table id="S11.Ex17" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S11.Ex17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{\underline{L}_{d}}:\operatorname{Ham}_{c}(\mathbb{D})\rightarrow\mathbb{R}\qquad\varphi_{G}^{1}\mapsto c_{\underline{L}_{d}}(G)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><msub><munder accentunder="true"><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><mi>d</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Ham</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝔻</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:2em;" width="2em"></mspace><mrow><msubsup><mi>φ</mi><mi>G</mi><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><msub><munder accentunder="true"><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><mi>d</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{\underline{L}_{d}}:\operatorname{Ham}_{c}(\mathbb{D})\rightarrow\mathbb{R}\qquad\varphi_{G}^{1}\mapsto c_{\underline{L}_{d}}(G)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S11.p10.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S11.p10.3.1" class="ltx_text">is uniformly continuous with respect to the <math id="S11.p10.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C^{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>C</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C^{0}</annotation></semantics></math> topology on <math id="S11.p10.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{Ham}_{c}(\mathbb{D})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Ham</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝔻</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{Ham}_{c}(\mathbb{D})</annotation></semantics></math> and continuously extends to a map <math id="S11.p10.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{\underline{L}_{d}}:\operatorname{Homeo}_{c}(\mathbb{D})\rightarrow\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><msub><munder accentunder="true"><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><mi>d</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Homeo</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝔻</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{\underline{L}_{d}}:\operatorname{Homeo}_{c}(\mathbb{D})\rightarrow\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math>, see <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bibx33" title="" class="ltx_ref">CHMSS22</a>, Proposition 3.4]</cite>. We have</span></p>
<table id="S11.E4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(11.4)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S11.E4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{\underline{L}_{d}}(\varphi_{H}^{1})=\lim_{k\rightarrow\infty}f_{\underline{L}_{d}}(\varphi_{H_{k}}^{1})=\lim_{k\rightarrow\infty}c_{\underline{L}_{d}}(H_{k})=c_{\underline{L}_{d}}(H)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><msub><munder accentunder="true"><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><mi>d</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>φ</mi><mi>H</mi><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">lim</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><msub><munder accentunder="true"><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><mi>d</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>φ</mi><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">lim</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><msub><munder accentunder="true"><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><mi>d</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><msub><munder accentunder="true"><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><mi>d</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{\underline{L}_{d}}(\varphi_{H}^{1})=\lim_{k\rightarrow\infty}f_{\underline{L}_{d}}(\varphi_{H_{k}}^{1})=\lim_{k\rightarrow\infty}c_{\underline{L}_{d}}(H_{k})=c_{\underline{L}_{d}}(H).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S11.p10.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="S11.p10.4.1" class="ltx_text">The map <math id="S11.p10.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{\underline{L}_{d}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>f</mi><msub><munder accentunder="true"><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><mi>d</mi></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{\underline{L}_{d}}</annotation></semantics></math> is a quasimorphism with defect at most <math id="S11.p10.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{A}{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><mi>A</mi><mi>d</mi></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{A}{d}</annotation></semantics></math>, see <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bibx33" title="" class="ltx_ref">CHMSS22</a>, Proof of Proposition 7.9]</cite>. It is proved in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bibx33" title="" class="ltx_ref">CHMSS22</a>, Theorem 7.7]</cite> that the homogenization</span></p>
<table id="S11.Ex18" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S11.Ex18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{d}:\operatorname{Homeo}_{c}(\mathbb{D})\rightarrow\mathbb{R}\qquad f_{d}(\varphi)\coloneqq\lim_{n\rightarrow\infty}\frac{f_{\underline{L}_{d}}(\varphi^{n})}{n}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Homeo</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝔻</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:2em;" width="2em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>φ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">≔</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">lim</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></munder><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><msub><munder accentunder="true"><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><mi>d</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>φ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{d}:\operatorname{Homeo}_{c}(\mathbb{D})\rightarrow\mathbb{R}\qquad f_{d}(\varphi)\coloneqq\lim_{n\rightarrow\infty}\frac{f_{\underline{L}_{d}}(\varphi^{n})}{n}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S11.p10.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="S11.p10.5.1" class="ltx_text">is independent of the monotone <math id="S11.p10.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math>-component link <math id="S11.p10.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underline{L}_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><munder accentunder="true"><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><mi>d</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underline{L}_{d}</annotation></semantics></math>. A simple computation using the fact that <math id="S11.p10.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{\underline{L}_{d}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>f</mi><msub><munder accentunder="true"><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><mi>d</mi></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{\underline{L}_{d}}</annotation></semantics></math> has defect at most <math id="S11.p10.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{A}{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><mi>A</mi><mi>d</mi></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{A}{d}</annotation></semantics></math> shows that <math id="S11.p10.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|f_{d}-f_{\underline{L}_{d}}|\leq\frac{A}{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><msub><munder accentunder="true"><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><mi>d</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><mi>A</mi><mi>d</mi></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|f_{d}-f_{\underline{L}_{d}}|\leq\frac{A}{d}</annotation></semantics></math>. We deduce that <math id="S11.p10.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|f_{\underline{L}_{d}}-f_{\underline{L}_{d}^{\prime}}|\leq\frac{2A}{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><msub><munder accentunder="true"><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><mi>d</mi></msub></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><msubsup><munder accentunder="true"><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><mi>d</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><mi>d</mi></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|f_{\underline{L}_{d}}-f_{\underline{L}_{d}^{\prime}}|\leq\frac{2A}{d}</annotation></semantics></math> for any other monotone <math id="S11.p10.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math>-component link <math id="S11.p10.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underline{L}_{d}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><munder accentunder="true"><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><mi>d</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underline{L}_{d}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>. In combination with (<a href="#S11.E4" title="In Proof. ‣ 11. 𝐶^{2-𝜀} failure of packing stability ‣ Packing stability and the subleading asymptotics of symplectic Weyl laws" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">11.4</span></a>), this implies inequality (<a href="#S11.E3" title="In Proof. ‣ 11. 𝐶^{2-𝜀} failure of packing stability ‣ Packing stability and the subleading asymptotics of symplectic Weyl laws" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">11.3</span></a>).</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S11.p11" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S11.p11.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S11.p11.1.1" class="ltx_text">Note that since <math id="S11.p11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi_{H}^{1}=\varphi_{\tilde{H}}^{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>φ</mi><mi>H</mi><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>φ</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>H</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi_{H}^{1}=\varphi_{\tilde{H}}^{1}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</span></p>
<table id="S11.Ex19" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S11.Ex19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{\underline{L}_{d}}(H)=f_{\underline{L}_{d}}(\varphi_{H}^{1})=f_{\underline{L}_{d}}(\varphi_{\tilde{H}}^{1})=c_{\underline{L}_{d}}(\tilde{H})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><msub><munder accentunder="true"><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><mi>d</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><msub><munder accentunder="true"><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><mi>d</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>φ</mi><mi>H</mi><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><msub><munder accentunder="true"><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><mi>d</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>φ</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>H</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><msub><munder accentunder="true"><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><mi>d</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>H</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{\underline{L}_{d}}(H)=f_{\underline{L}_{d}}(\varphi_{H}^{1})=f_{\underline{L}_{d}}(\varphi_{\tilde{H}}^{1})=c_{\underline{L}_{d}}(\tilde{H}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S11.p11.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S11.p11.2.1" class="ltx_text">Moreover,</span></p>
<table id="S11.Ex20" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S11.Ex20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\int_{[0,1]\times S^{2}}Hdt\wedge\omega=\int_{[0,1]\times S^{2}}\tilde{H}dt\wedge\omega." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></msub><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>∧</mo><mi>ω</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></msub><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>H</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>∧</mo><mi>ω</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\int_{[0,1]\times S^{2}}Hdt\wedge\omega=\int_{[0,1]\times S^{2}}\tilde{H}dt\wedge\omega.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S11.p11.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S11.p11.3.1" class="ltx_text">When checking (<a href="#S11.E2" title="In Lemma 11.5. ‣ 11. 𝐶^{2-𝜀} failure of packing stability ‣ Packing stability and the subleading asymptotics of symplectic Weyl laws" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">11.2</span></a>), we may therefore replace <math id="S11.p11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H</annotation></semantics></math> by the autonomous Hamiltonian <math id="S11.p11.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{H}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>H</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{H}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S11.p12" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S11.p12.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S11.p12.1.1" class="ltx_text">It remains to construct a special sequence of monotone links <math id="S11.p12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underline{L}_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><munder accentunder="true"><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><mi>d</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underline{L}_{d}</annotation></semantics></math> for which we can show (<a href="#S11.E2" title="In Lemma 11.5. ‣ 11. 𝐶^{2-𝜀} failure of packing stability ‣ Packing stability and the subleading asymptotics of symplectic Weyl laws" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">11.2</span></a>) to hold. Monotonicity means that each component of <math id="S11.p12.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S^{2}\setminus\underline{L}_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>S</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>∖</mo><msub><munder accentunder="true"><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S^{2}\setminus\underline{L}_{d}</annotation></semantics></math> must have area <math id="S11.p12.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{A}{d+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{A}{d+1}</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="S11.p12.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N=N(d)&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N=N(d)&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> be the maximal positive integer such that the area of <math id="S11.p12.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{N}^{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>D</mi><mi>N</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{N}^{i}</annotation></semantics></math> is at least <math id="S11.p12.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{A}{d+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{A}{d+1}</annotation></semantics></math>. For each of the disks <math id="S11.p12.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{n}^{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>D</mi><mi>n</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{n}^{i}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="S11.p12.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\leq N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\leq N</annotation></semantics></math>, we place <math id="S11.p12.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lfloor\operatorname{area}(D_{n}^{i})/\frac{A}{d+1}\rfloor" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>area</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>D</mi><mi>n</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mfrac><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌋</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lfloor\operatorname{area}(D_{n}^{i})/\frac{A}{d+1}\rfloor</annotation></semantics></math> components of <math id="S11.p12.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underline{L}_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><munder accentunder="true"><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><mi>d</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underline{L}_{d}</annotation></semantics></math> inside <math id="S11.p12.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{n}^{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>D</mi><mi>n</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{n}^{i}</annotation></semantics></math> such that they form a nested sequence of circles centered at the center of <math id="S11.p12.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{n}^{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>D</mi><mi>n</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{n}^{i}</annotation></semantics></math>. We adjust the radii of these circles such that the disk bounded by the innermost circle and the annuli bounded by two consecutive circles have area <math id="S11.p12.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{A}{d+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{A}{d+1}</annotation></semantics></math>. Note that since <math id="S11.p12.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math> was chosen to be supported inside <math id="S11.p12.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{D}_{\frac{1}{10}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝔻</mi><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>10</mn></mfrac></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{D}_{\frac{1}{10}}</annotation></semantics></math>, the outermost circle component of <math id="S11.p12.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underline{L}_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><munder accentunder="true"><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><mi>d</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underline{L}_{d}</annotation></semantics></math> in <math id="S11.p12.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{n}^{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>D</mi><mi>n</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{n}^{i}</annotation></semantics></math> is disjoint from the support of <math id="S11.p12.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{H}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>H</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{H}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S11.p13" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S11.p13.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S11.p13.1.1" class="ltx_text">We show that we can insert the remaining components of the link <math id="S11.p13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underline{L}_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><munder accentunder="true"><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><mi>d</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underline{L}_{d}</annotation></semantics></math> to be disjoint from the support of <math id="S11.p13.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{H}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>H</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{H}</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="S11.p13.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma</annotation></semantics></math> denote the surface obtained from <math id="S11.p13.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>S</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> be removing, for every disk <math id="S11.p13.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{n}^{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>D</mi><mi>n</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{n}^{i}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="S11.p13.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\leq N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\leq N</annotation></semantics></math>, the disk bounded by the outermost component of <math id="S11.p13.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underline{L}_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><munder accentunder="true"><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><mi>d</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underline{L}_{d}</annotation></semantics></math> inside <math id="S11.p13.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{n}^{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>D</mi><mi>n</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{n}^{i}</annotation></semantics></math>. We place the remaining components of <math id="S11.p13.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underline{L}_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><munder accentunder="true"><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><mi>d</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underline{L}_{d}</annotation></semantics></math> inside <math id="S11.p13.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma</annotation></semantics></math> such that each of them bounds a topological disk <math id="S11.p13.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>D</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D</annotation></semantics></math> of area <math id="S11.p13.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{A}{d+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{A}{d+1}</annotation></semantics></math>. As a first step, we arrange the components such that for each of the resulting disks <math id="S11.p13.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>D</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D</annotation></semantics></math>, the total area of all disks <math id="S11.p13.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{n}^{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>D</mi><mi>n</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{n}^{i}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="S11.p13.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n&gt;N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n&gt;N</annotation></semantics></math> intersecting <math id="S11.p13.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>D</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D</annotation></semantics></math> is at most <math id="S11.p13.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{16A}{d+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><mrow><mn>16</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{16A}{d+1}</annotation></semantics></math>. This is not particularly subtle. For example, it is enough to make sure that each of the topological disks <math id="S11.p13.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>D</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D</annotation></semantics></math> is contained in a metric disk of area <math id="S11.p13.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{4A}{d+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{4A}{d+1}</annotation></semantics></math>, where we use the standard metric on <math id="S11.p13.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝔻</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{D}</annotation></semantics></math>. We can also make sure that each component of <math id="S11.p13.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underline{L}_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><munder accentunder="true"><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><mi>d</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underline{L}_{d}</annotation></semantics></math> only intersects finitely many of the disks <math id="S11.p13.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{n}^{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>D</mi><mi>n</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{n}^{i}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S11.p14" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S11.p14.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S11.p14.1.1" class="ltx_text">Our second step is to move the link <math id="S11.p14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underline{L}_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><munder accentunder="true"><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><mi>d</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underline{L}_{d}</annotation></semantics></math> via a compactly supported Hamiltonian diffeomorphism of <math id="S11.p14.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma</annotation></semantics></math> to make it disjoint from the support of <math id="S11.p14.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{H}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>H</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{H}</annotation></semantics></math>. For each disk <math id="S11.p14.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{n}^{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>D</mi><mi>n</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{n}^{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, let <math id="S11.p14.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{D}_{n}^{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>D</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>n</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{D}_{n}^{i}</annotation></semantics></math> be the disk with the same center as <math id="S11.p14.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{n}^{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>D</mi><mi>n</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{n}^{i}</annotation></semantics></math> and with radius <math id="S11.p14.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{r_{n}}{10}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mn>10</mn></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{r_{n}}{10}</annotation></semantics></math>. Note that <math id="S11.p14.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{H}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>H</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{H}</annotation></semantics></math> is supported in the closure of the union of all <math id="S11.p14.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{D}_{n}^{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>D</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>n</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{D}_{n}^{i}</annotation></semantics></math>. Moreover, note that for each component <math id="S11.p14.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="S11.p14.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underline{L}_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><munder accentunder="true"><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><mi>d</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underline{L}_{d}</annotation></semantics></math>, the total area of all disks <math id="S11.p14.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{D}_{n}^{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>D</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>n</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{D}_{n}^{i}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="S11.p14.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n&gt;N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n&gt;N</annotation></semantics></math> intersecting the disk bounded by <math id="S11.p14.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math> is strictly less than <math id="S11.p14.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{A}{d+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{A}{d+1}</annotation></semantics></math>. We can therefore find a compactly supported Hamiltonian diffeomorphism <math id="S11.p14.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ψ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="S11.p14.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma</annotation></semantics></math> which moves every disk <math id="S11.p14.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{D}_{n}^{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>D</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>n</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{D}_{n}^{i}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="S11.p14.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n&gt;N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n&gt;N</annotation></semantics></math> intersecting <math id="S11.p14.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underline{L}_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><munder accentunder="true"><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><mi>d</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underline{L}_{d}</annotation></semantics></math> into the interior of the disk bounded by some component <math id="S11.p14.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="S11.p14.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underline{L}_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><munder accentunder="true"><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><mi>d</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underline{L}_{d}</annotation></semantics></math> it intersects. Moreover, we can choose <math id="S11.p14.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ψ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi</annotation></semantics></math> such that it does not move any disk <math id="S11.p14.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{D}_{n}^{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>D</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>n</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{D}_{n}^{i}</annotation></semantics></math> which does not intersect <math id="S11.p14.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underline{L}_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><munder accentunder="true"><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><mi>d</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underline{L}_{d}</annotation></semantics></math>. After replacing <math id="S11.p14.m26" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underline{L}_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><munder accentunder="true"><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><mi>d</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underline{L}_{d}</annotation></semantics></math> by <math id="S11.p14.m27" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi^{-1}(\underline{L}_{d})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>ψ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><munder accentunder="true"><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><mi>d</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi^{-1}(\underline{L}_{d})</annotation></semantics></math>, we can assume that <math id="S11.p14.m28" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underline{L}_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><munder accentunder="true"><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><mi>d</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underline{L}_{d}</annotation></semantics></math> is disjoint from the support of <math id="S11.p14.m29" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{H}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>H</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{H}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S11.p15" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S11.p15.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S11.p15.1.1" class="ltx_text">We observe that each component of <math id="S11.p15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underline{L}_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><munder accentunder="true"><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><mi>d</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underline{L}_{d}</annotation></semantics></math> is contained in a level set of <math id="S11.p15.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{H}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>H</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{H}</annotation></semantics></math>. One can therefore easily compute <math id="S11.p15.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{\underline{L}_{d}}(\tilde{H})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><msub><munder accentunder="true"><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><mi>d</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>H</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{\underline{L}_{d}}(\tilde{H})</annotation></semantics></math> via the Lagrangian control property in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bibx33" title="" class="ltx_ref">CHMSS22</a>, Theorem 1.13]</cite>. For each component <math id="S11.p15.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="S11.p15.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underline{L}_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><munder accentunder="true"><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><mi>d</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underline{L}_{d}</annotation></semantics></math>, let <math id="S11.p15.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{H}|_{L}\in\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>H</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mi>L</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{H}|_{L}\in\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math> be the value <math id="S11.p15.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{H}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>H</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{H}</annotation></semantics></math> takes on <math id="S11.p15.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math>. Then</span></p>
<table id="S11.E5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(11.5)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S11.E5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{\underline{L}_{d}}(\tilde{H})=\frac{1}{d}\sum_{L\subset\underline{L}_{d}}\tilde{H}|_{L}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><msub><munder accentunder="true"><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><mi>d</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>H</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>d</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⊂</mo><msub><munder accentunder="true"><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow></munder><msub><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>H</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mi>L</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{\underline{L}_{d}}(\tilde{H})=\frac{1}{d}\sum_{L\subset\underline{L}_{d}}\tilde{H}|_{L}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S11.p15.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S11.p15.2.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="S11.p15.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underline{L}_{d}^{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><munder accentunder="true"><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underline{L}_{d}^{+}</annotation></semantics></math> be the collection of all components of <math id="S11.p15.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underline{L}_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><munder accentunder="true"><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><mi>d</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underline{L}_{d}</annotation></semantics></math> which are contained in a disk <math id="S11.p15.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{n}^{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>D</mi><mi>n</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{n}^{i}</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="S11.p15.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\leq N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\leq N</annotation></semantics></math>. By construction of <math id="S11.p15.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underline{L}_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><munder accentunder="true"><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><mi>d</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underline{L}_{d}</annotation></semantics></math>, only components <math id="S11.p15.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L\subset\underline{L}_{d}^{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⊂</mo><msubsup><munder accentunder="true"><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L\subset\underline{L}_{d}^{+}</annotation></semantics></math> contribute to the sum (<a href="#S11.E5" title="In Proof. ‣ 11. 𝐶^{2-𝜀} failure of packing stability ‣ Packing stability and the subleading asymptotics of symplectic Weyl laws" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">11.5</span></a>).</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S11.p16" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S11.p16.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S11.p16.1.1" class="ltx_text">Consider a disk <math id="S11.p16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{n}^{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>D</mi><mi>n</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{n}^{i}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="S11.p16.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\leq N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\leq N</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="S11.p16.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{1},\dots,L_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{1},\dots,L_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the components of <math id="S11.p16.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underline{L}_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><munder accentunder="true"><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><mi>d</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underline{L}_{d}</annotation></semantics></math> inside <math id="S11.p16.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{n}^{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>D</mi><mi>n</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{n}^{i}</annotation></semantics></math>. Suppose that they are ordered such that <math id="S11.p16.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> is inside <math id="S11.p16.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="S11.p16.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i&lt;j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i&lt;j</annotation></semantics></math>. We claim that</span></p>
<table id="S11.E6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(11.6)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S11.E6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{A}{d+1}\sum\limits_{i=1}^{k}\tilde{H}|_{L_{i}}\leq\int_{D_{n}^{i}}\tilde{H}\omega." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>k</mi></munderover><msub><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>H</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">≤</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∫</mo><msubsup><mi>D</mi><mi>n</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup></msub><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>H</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ω</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{A}{d+1}\sum\limits_{i=1}^{k}\tilde{H}|_{L_{i}}\leq\int_{D_{n}^{i}}\tilde{H}\omega.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S11.p16.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S11.p16.2.1" class="ltx_text">Indeed, let <math id="S11.p16.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math> be the function on <math id="S11.p16.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{n}^{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>D</mi><mi>n</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{n}^{i}</annotation></semantics></math> whose value on the disk bounded by <math id="S11.p16.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> is equal to <math id="S11.p16.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{H}|_{L_{1}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>H</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{H}|_{L_{1}}</annotation></semantics></math>, whose value on the annulus between <math id="S11.p16.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S11.p16.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{i+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>L</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{i+1}</annotation></semantics></math> is equal to <math id="S11.p16.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{H}|_{L_{i+1}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>H</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{H}|_{L_{i+1}}</annotation></semantics></math>, and which vanishes outside of <math id="S11.p16.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>. Since the function <math id="S11.p16.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math> was chosen to be non-increasing in the radial direction, we have <math id="S11.p16.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G\leq\tilde{H}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>≤</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>H</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G\leq\tilde{H}</annotation></semantics></math>. Moreover, the left hand side of (<a href="#S11.E6" title="In Proof. ‣ 11. 𝐶^{2-𝜀} failure of packing stability ‣ Packing stability and the subleading asymptotics of symplectic Weyl laws" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">11.6</span></a>) is simply the integral of <math id="S11.p16.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math> over <math id="S11.p16.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{n}^{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>D</mi><mi>n</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{n}^{i}</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus identity (<a href="#S11.E6" title="In Proof. ‣ 11. 𝐶^{2-𝜀} failure of packing stability ‣ Packing stability and the subleading asymptotics of symplectic Weyl laws" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">11.6</span></a>) is an immediate consequence.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S11.p17" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S11.p17.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S11.p17.1.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="S11.p17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{d}^{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>D</mi><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{d}^{+}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the union of all disks <math id="S11.p17.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{n}^{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>D</mi><mi>n</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{n}^{i}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="S11.p17.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\leq N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\leq N</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S11.p17.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{d}^{-}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>D</mi><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{d}^{-}</annotation></semantics></math> the union of all disks <math id="S11.p17.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{n}^{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>D</mi><mi>n</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{n}^{i}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="S11.p17.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n&gt;N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n&gt;N</annotation></semantics></math>. Then we can estimate using (<a href="#S11.E6" title="In Proof. ‣ 11. 𝐶^{2-𝜀} failure of packing stability ‣ Packing stability and the subleading asymptotics of symplectic Weyl laws" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">11.6</span></a>):</span></p>
<table id="S11.EGx7" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S11.Ex21"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S11.Ex21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle dc_{\underline{L}_{d}}(\tilde{H})-dA^{-1}\int_{\mathbb{D}}\tilde{H}\omega" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><msub><munder accentunder="true"><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><mi>d</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>H</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><mi>𝔻</mi></msub></mstyle><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>H</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ω</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle dc_{\underline{L}_{d}}(\tilde{H})-dA^{-1}\int_{\mathbb{D}}\tilde{H}\omega</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S11.Ex21.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum\limits_{L\subset\underline{L}_{d}^{+}}\tilde{H}|_{L}-dA^{-1}\int_{D_{d}^{+}}\tilde{H}\omega-dA^{-1}\int_{D_{d}^{-}}\tilde{H}\omega" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⊂</mo><msubsup><munder accentunder="true"><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup></mrow></munder></mstyle><msub><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>H</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mi>L</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><msubsup><mi>D</mi><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup></msub></mstyle><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>H</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ω</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><msubsup><mi>D</mi><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo></msubsup></msub></mstyle><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>H</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ω</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum\limits_{L\subset\underline{L}_{d}^{+}}\tilde{H}|_{L}-dA^{-1}\int_{D_{d}^{+}}\tilde{H}\omega-dA^{-1}\int_{D_{d}^{-}}\tilde{H}\omega</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S11.Ex22"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S11.Ex22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq(d+1)A^{-1}\int_{D_{d}^{+}}\tilde{H}\omega-dA^{-1}\int_{D_{d}^{+}}\tilde{H}\omega-dA^{-1}\int_{D_{d}^{-}}\tilde{H}\omega" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><msubsup><mi>D</mi><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup></msub></mstyle><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>H</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ω</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><msubsup><mi>D</mi><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup></msub></mstyle><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>H</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ω</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><msubsup><mi>D</mi><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo></msubsup></msub></mstyle><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>H</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ω</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq(d+1)A^{-1}\int_{D_{d}^{+}}\tilde{H}\omega-dA^{-1}\int_{D_{d}^{+}}\tilde{H}\omega-dA^{-1}\int_{D_{d}^{-}}\tilde{H}\omega</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S11.Ex23"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S11.Ex23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq A^{-1}\int_{\mathbb{D}}\tilde{H}\omega-dA^{-1}\int_{D_{d}^{-}}\tilde{H}\omega." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><mi>𝔻</mi></msub></mstyle><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>H</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ω</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><msubsup><mi>D</mi><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo></msubsup></msub></mstyle><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>H</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ω</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq A^{-1}\int_{\mathbb{D}}\tilde{H}\omega-dA^{-1}\int_{D_{d}^{-}}\tilde{H}\omega.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S11.p17.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S11.p17.2.1" class="ltx_text">Therefore, it suffices to show that <math id="S11.p17.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d\int_{D_{d}^{-}}\tilde{H}\omega" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∫</mo><msubsup><mi>D</mi><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo></msubsup></msub><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>H</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ω</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d\int_{D_{d}^{-}}\tilde{H}\omega</annotation></semantics></math> diverges to <math id="S11.p17.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="+\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">+\infty</annotation></semantics></math> as <math id="S11.p17.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math> tends to infinity. By construction of <math id="S11.p17.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{H}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>H</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{H}</annotation></semantics></math> we have</span></p>
<table id="S11.EGx8" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S11.Ex24"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S11.Ex24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle d\int_{D_{d}^{-}}\tilde{H}\omega" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><msubsup><mi>D</mi><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo></msubsup></msub></mstyle><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>H</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ω</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle d\int_{D_{d}^{-}}\tilde{H}\omega</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S11.Ex24.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=d\sum\limits_{n&gt;N(d)}n\int_{\mathbb{D}_{r_{n}}}f_{n}\omega" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><msub><mi>𝔻</mi><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msub></msub></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ω</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=d\sum\limits_{n&gt;N(d)}n\int_{\mathbb{D}_{r_{n}}}f_{n}\omega</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S11.Ex25"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S11.Ex25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=d\sum\limits_{n&gt;N(d)}\frac{n\ln(n)r_{n}^{2}}{n^{2}}\int_{\mathbb{D}}f\omega" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><mi>𝔻</mi></msub></mstyle><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ω</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=d\sum\limits_{n&gt;N(d)}\frac{n\ln(n)r_{n}^{2}}{n^{2}}\int_{\mathbb{D}}f\omega</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S11.Ex26"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S11.Ex26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=d\sum\limits_{n&gt;N(d)}\frac{1}{n^{3}\ln(n)^{3}}\int_{\mathbb{D}}f\omega." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo>⁡</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><mi>𝔻</mi></msub></mstyle><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ω</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=d\sum\limits_{n&gt;N(d)}\frac{1}{n^{3}\ln(n)^{3}}\int_{\mathbb{D}}f\omega.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S11.p17.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S11.p17.3.1" class="ltx_text">We estimate</span></p>
<table id="S11.EGx9" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S11.Ex27"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S11.Ex27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle d\sum\limits_{n&gt;N(d)}\frac{1}{n^{3}\ln(n)^{3}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo>⁡</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle d\sum\limits_{n&gt;N(d)}\frac{1}{n^{3}\ln(n)^{3}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S11.Ex27.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\geq d\int_{N(d)+1}^{\infty}\frac{1}{x^{3}\ln(x)^{3}}dx" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo>⁡</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\geq d\int_{N(d)+1}^{\infty}\frac{1}{x^{3}\ln(x)^{3}}dx</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S11.Ex28"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S11.Ex28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=d\int_{\ln(N(d)+1)}^{\infty}u^{-3}e^{-2u}du" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><msup><mi>u</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=d\int_{\ln(N(d)+1)}^{\infty}u^{-3}e^{-2u}du</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S11.Ex29"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S11.Ex29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=d(N(d)+1)^{-2}\int_{0}^{\infty}\frac{1}{(v+\ln(N(d)+1))^{3}}e^{-2v}dv" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>3</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=d(N(d)+1)^{-2}\int_{0}^{\infty}\frac{1}{(v+\ln(N(d)+1))^{3}}e^{-2v}dv</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S11.Ex30"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S11.Ex30.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=d(N(d)+1)^{-2}\ln(N(d)+1)^{-3}\int_{0}^{\infty}\frac{1}{(1+\frac{v}{\ln(N(d)+1)})^{3}}e^{-2v}dv" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo>⁡</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>3</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=d(N(d)+1)^{-2}\ln(N(d)+1)^{-3}\int_{0}^{\infty}\frac{1}{(1+\frac{v}{\ln(N(d)+1)})^{3}}e^{-2v}dv</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S11.Ex31"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S11.Ex31.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\geq CdN(d)^{-2}\ln(N(d))^{-3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo>⁡</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\geq CdN(d)^{-2}\ln(N(d))^{-3}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S11.p17.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="S11.p17.4.1" class="ltx_text">for some constant <math id="S11.p17.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> which can be chosen uniformly among all sufficiently large <math id="S11.p17.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math>. Recall that <math id="S11.p17.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N(d)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N(d)</annotation></semantics></math> is the maximal integer <math id="S11.p17.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> such that the area of <math id="S11.p17.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{n}^{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>D</mi><mi>n</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{n}^{i}</annotation></semantics></math> is at least <math id="S11.p17.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{A}{d+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{A}{d+1}</annotation></semantics></math>. This means that</span></p>
<table id="S11.Ex32" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S11.Ex32.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi N(d)^{-2}\ln(N(d))^{-4}\geq\frac{A}{d+1}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo>⁡</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mfrac><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi N(d)^{-2}\ln(N(d))^{-4}\geq\frac{A}{d+1}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S11.p17.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="S11.p17.5.1" class="ltx_text">We can therefore further estimate</span></p>
<table id="S11.Ex33" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S11.Ex33.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="dN(d)^{-2}\ln(N(d))^{-3}\geq C\ln(N(d))." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo>⁡</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">dN(d)^{-2}\ln(N(d))^{-3}\geq C\ln(N(d)).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S11.p17.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="S11.p17.6.1" class="ltx_text">Since <math id="S11.p17.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N(d)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N(d)</annotation></semantics></math> tends to infinity as <math id="S11.p17.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math> goes to infinity, we conclude that <math id="S11.p17.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d\int_{D_{d}^{-}}\tilde{H}\omega" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∫</mo><msubsup><mi>D</mi><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo></msubsup></msub><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>H</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ω</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d\int_{D_{d}^{-}}\tilde{H}\omega</annotation></semantics></math> diverges to <math id="S11.p17.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="+\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">+\infty</annotation></semantics></math> as <math id="S11.p17.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math> goes to infinity.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S11.p18" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S11.p18.1" class="ltx_p">Our next step is to use Chen’s work <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bibx20" title="" class="ltx_ref">Chea</a>, <a href="#bib.bibx21" title="" class="ltx_ref">Cheb</a>]</cite> relating PFH and link spectral invariants to obtain information on the subleading asymptotics of the PFH spectral invariants of <math id="S11.p18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H</annotation></semantics></math>. Recall from <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bibx45" title="" class="ltx_ref">EH</a>]</cite> that for every area preserving map <math id="S11.p18.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi\in\operatorname{Diff}(S^{2},\omega)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>Diff</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi\in\operatorname{Diff}(S^{2},\omega)</annotation></semantics></math>, every reference cycle <math id="S11.p18.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma\subset Y_{\phi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>⊂</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma\subset Y_{\phi}</annotation></semantics></math> in the mapping torus <math id="S11.p18.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y_{\phi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y_{\phi}</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="S11.p18.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϕ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi</annotation></semantics></math>, and every non-zero PFH class <math id="S11.p18.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma\in HP(\phi,\gamma)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma\in HP(\phi,\gamma)</annotation></semantics></math>, we have a spectral invariant</p>
<table id="S11.Ex34" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S11.Ex34.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C^{\infty}(Y_{\phi})\rightarrow\mathbb{R}\qquad G\mapsto c_{\sigma}(\phi,\gamma,G)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>C</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow><mspace style="width:2em;" width="2em"></mspace><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>σ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C^{\infty}(Y_{\phi})\rightarrow\mathbb{R}\qquad G\mapsto c_{\sigma}(\phi,\gamma,G).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S11.p18.2" class="ltx_p">Similarly to the case of link spectral invariants, this map is Lipschitz continuous with respect to the <math id="S11.p18.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C^{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>C</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C^{0}</annotation></semantics></math> norm on <math id="S11.p18.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C^{\infty}(Y_{\phi})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>C</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C^{\infty}(Y_{\phi})</annotation></semantics></math> and continuously extends to <math id="S11.p18.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C^{0}(Y_{\phi})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>C</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C^{0}(Y_{\phi})</annotation></semantics></math>. Chen considers the special case <math id="S11.p18.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi=\operatorname{id}_{S^{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>id</mi><msup><mi>S</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi=\operatorname{id}_{S^{2}}</annotation></semantics></math>. In this case, the mapping torus <math id="S11.p18.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y_{\phi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y_{\phi}</annotation></semantics></math> is simply given by <math id="S11.p18.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{T}\times S^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝕋</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{T}\times S^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>. For every <math id="S11.p18.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math>, Chen considers the special reference cycle <math id="S11.p18.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma_{d}\coloneqq d\cdot(\mathbb{T}\times\left\{*\right\})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝕋</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∗</mo><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma_{d}\coloneqq d\cdot(\mathbb{T}\times\left\{*\right\})</annotation></semantics></math>, i.e. <math id="S11.p18.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math> copies of the circle <math id="S11.p18.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{T}\times\left\{*\right\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝕋</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∗</mo><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{T}\times\left\{*\right\}</annotation></semantics></math> for some point <math id="S11.p18.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="*\in S^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∗</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">*\in S^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>. For each <math id="S11.p18.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math>, he constructs a distinguished non-zero class <math id="S11.p18.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e_{d}\in HP(\operatorname{id}_{S^{2}},\gamma_{d})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>id</mi><msup><mi>S</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e_{d}\in HP(\operatorname{id}_{S^{2}},\gamma_{d})</annotation></semantics></math> called the “PFH unit”. Let <math id="S11.p18.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underline{L}_{d}\subset S^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><munder accentunder="true"><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><mi>d</mi></msub><mo>⊂</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underline{L}_{d}\subset S^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> be a monotone <math id="S11.p18.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math>-component link. Suppose that every component of <math id="S11.p18.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underline{L}_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><munder accentunder="true"><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><mi>d</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underline{L}_{d}</annotation></semantics></math> bounds a disk in <math id="S11.p18.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>S</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> of area <math id="S11.p18.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{A}{d+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{A}{d+1}</annotation></semantics></math>. For such links <math id="S11.p18.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underline{L}_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><munder accentunder="true"><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><mi>d</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underline{L}_{d}</annotation></semantics></math>, Chen shows that</p>
<table id="S11.E7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(11.7)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S11.E7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{e_{d}}(\operatorname{id}_{S^{2}},\gamma_{d},G)+\int_{\gamma_{d}}Gdt-A\leq dc_{\underline{L}_{d}}(G)\leq c_{e_{d}}(\operatorname{id}_{S^{2}},\gamma_{d},G)+\int_{\gamma_{d}}Gdt" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>id</mi><msup><mi>S</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∫</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></msub><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><msub><munder accentunder="true"><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><mi>d</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>id</mi><msup><mi>S</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∫</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></msub><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{e_{d}}(\operatorname{id}_{S^{2}},\gamma_{d},G)+\int_{\gamma_{d}}Gdt-A\leq dc_{\underline{L}_{d}}(G)\leq c_{e_{d}}(\operatorname{id}_{S^{2}},\gamma_{d},G)+\int_{\gamma_{d}}Gdt</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S11.p18.3" class="ltx_p">for every <math id="S11.p18.m26" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math>-periodic Hamiltonian <math id="S11.p18.m27" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math> on <math id="S11.p18.m28" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>S</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S11.Thmtheorem7" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_remark">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S11.Thmtheorem7.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Remark 11.7</span></span><span id="S11.Thmtheorem7.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S11.Thmtheorem7.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S11.Thmtheorem7.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In (<a href="#S11.E7" title="In 11. 𝐶^{2-𝜀} failure of packing stability ‣ Packing stability and the subleading asymptotics of symplectic Weyl laws" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">11.7</span></a>) we follow the notations and conventions for PFH and link spectral invariants introduced in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bibx45" title="" class="ltx_ref">EH</a>]</cite> and <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bibx33" title="" class="ltx_ref">CHMSS22</a>]</cite>. These differ slightly from the ones used by Chen. Most notably, Chen’s definition of link spectral invariants differs from the one used in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bibx33" title="" class="ltx_ref">CHMSS22</a>]</cite> by a factor <math id="S11.Thmtheorem7.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math>. For this reason, the factor <math id="S11.Thmtheorem7.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math> in front of the link spectral invariant in (<a href="#S11.E7" title="In 11. 𝐶^{2-𝜀} failure of packing stability ‣ Packing stability and the subleading asymptotics of symplectic Weyl laws" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">11.7</span></a>) does not show up in Chen’s work. Moreover, Chen normalizes surfaces to have area <math id="S11.Thmtheorem7.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus the summand <math id="S11.Thmtheorem7.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-A</annotation></semantics></math> becomes <math id="S11.Thmtheorem7.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-1</annotation></semantics></math> in Chen’s work.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S11.Thmtheorem8" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S11.Thmtheorem8.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 11.8</span></span><span id="S11.Thmtheorem8.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S11.Thmtheorem8.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S11.Thmtheorem8.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S11.Thmtheorem8.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">We have</span></p>
<table id="S11.Ex35" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S11.Ex35.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{e_{d}}(\operatorname{id}_{S^{2}},\gamma_{d},H)+\int_{\gamma_{d}}H-dA^{-1}\int_{[0,1]\times S^{2}}Hdt\wedge\omega\rightarrow-\infty\quad(d\rightarrow\infty)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>id</mi><msup><mi>S</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∫</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></msub><mi>H</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></msub><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>∧</mo><mi>ω</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{e_{d}}(\operatorname{id}_{S^{2}},\gamma_{d},H)+\int_{\gamma_{d}}H-dA^{-1}\int_{[0,1]\times S^{2}}Hdt\wedge\omega\rightarrow-\infty\quad(d\rightarrow\infty).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S11.4" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S11.p19" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S11.p19.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S11.p19.1.1" class="ltx_text">This is an immediate consequence of Lemma <a href="#S11.Thmtheorem5" title="Lemma 11.5. ‣ 11. 𝐶^{2-𝜀} failure of packing stability ‣ Packing stability and the subleading asymptotics of symplectic Weyl laws" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">11.5</span></a> and Chen’s inequalities (<a href="#S11.E7" title="In 11. 𝐶^{2-𝜀} failure of packing stability ‣ Packing stability and the subleading asymptotics of symplectic Weyl laws" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">11.7</span></a>).
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S11.p20" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S11.p20.1" class="ltx_p">Consider <math id="S11.p20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}\times\mathbb{T}\times S^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℝ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>𝕋</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}\times\mathbb{T}\times S^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> equipped with the symplectic form <math id="S11.p20.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="ds\wedge dt+\omega" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo>∧</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>ω</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">ds\wedge dt+\omega</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="S11.p20.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M\coloneqq D(H+A)\subset\mathbb{R}\times\mathbb{T}\times S^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⊂</mo><mrow><mi>ℝ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>𝕋</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M\coloneqq D(H+A)\subset\mathbb{R}\times\mathbb{T}\times S^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> be the symplectic cobordism between the graph of <math id="S11.p20.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H+A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H+A</annotation></semantics></math> and the graph of the Hamiltonian which is constant equal to <math id="S11.p20.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math>. It follows from (<a href="#S11.E1" title="In 11. 𝐶^{2-𝜀} failure of packing stability ‣ Packing stability and the subleading asymptotics of symplectic Weyl laws" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">11.1</span></a>) that the volume of <math id="S11.p20.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math> agrees with the volume of the disjoint union of <math id="S11.p20.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X(H)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X(H)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S11.p20.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B^{4}(A)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>B</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B^{4}(A)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S11.Thmtheorem9" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S11.Thmtheorem9.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 11.9</span></span><span id="S11.Thmtheorem9.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S11.Thmtheorem9.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S11.Thmtheorem9.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S11.Thmtheorem9.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Every compact subset of the disjoint union of the interiors of <math id="S11.Thmtheorem9.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X(H)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X(H)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S11.Thmtheorem9.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B^{4}(A)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>B</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B^{4}(A)</annotation></semantics></math> admits a symplectic embedding into the interior of <math id="S11.Thmtheorem9.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S11.Thmtheorem10" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_remark">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S11.Thmtheorem10.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Remark 11.10</span></span><span id="S11.Thmtheorem10.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S11.Thmtheorem10.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S11.Thmtheorem10.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Using the notation introduced in Theorem <a href="#Thmintrothm3" title="Theorem C (𝐶^{2-𝜀} failure of packing stability). ‣ 1.3. Limits of packing stability ‣ 1. Introduction ‣ Packing stability and the subleading asymptotics of symplectic Weyl laws" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C</span></a>, this statement is equivalent to the assertion that <math id="S11.Thmtheorem10.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p^{X(H)\sqcup B^{4}(A)}(M)=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>p</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⊔</mo><mrow><msup><mi>B</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p^{X(H)\sqcup B^{4}(A)}(M)=1</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S11.5" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S11.p21" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S11.p21.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S11.p21.1.1" class="ltx_text">Note that the domain <math id="S11.p21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U(H)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U(H)</annotation></semantics></math> showing up in the definition of <math id="S11.p21.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X(H)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X(H)</annotation></semantics></math> is contained in <math id="S11.p21.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}\times\mathbb{T}\times\operatorname{int}(\mathbb{D})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℝ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>𝕋</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mi>int</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝔻</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}\times\mathbb{T}\times\operatorname{int}(\mathbb{D})</annotation></semantics></math> and can therefore be naturally regarded as a subset of <math id="S11.p21.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}\times\mathbb{T}\times S^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℝ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>𝕋</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}\times\mathbb{T}\times S^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>. It is straightforward to check that translating <math id="S11.p21.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U(H)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U(H)</annotation></semantics></math> by <math id="S11.p21.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math> along the <math id="S11.p21.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ℝ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math> factor of <math id="S11.p21.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}\times\mathbb{T}\times S^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℝ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>𝕋</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}\times\mathbb{T}\times S^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> yields a domain contained in <math id="S11.p21.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{int}(M)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>int</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{int}(M)</annotation></semantics></math>. In other words, <math id="S11.p21.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U(H)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U(H)</annotation></semantics></math> symplectically embeds into <math id="S11.p21.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{int}(M)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>int</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{int}(M)</annotation></semantics></math>. The complement of the image of this symplectic embedding contains the set</span></p>
<table id="S11.Ex36" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S11.Ex36.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="W\coloneqq\left\{(s,t,z)\in\mathbb{R}\times\mathbb{T}\times\operatorname{int}(\mathbb{D})\mid z\in\operatorname{int}(\mathbb{D}),0&lt;s&lt;A|z|^{2}\right\}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℝ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>𝕋</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>int</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝔻</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>int</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝔻</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>A</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>z</mi><msup><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>}</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W\coloneqq\left\{(s,t,z)\in\mathbb{R}\times\mathbb{T}\times\operatorname{int}(\mathbb{D})\mid z\in\operatorname{int}(\mathbb{D}),0&lt;s&lt;A|z|^{2}\right\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S11.p21.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S11.p21.2.1" class="ltx_text">We claim that the interior of the ball <math id="S11.p21.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B(A)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B(A)</annotation></semantics></math> admits a symplectic embedding into <math id="S11.p21.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>W</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W</annotation></semantics></math>. Indeed, let <math id="S11.p21.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> denote the triangle in the first quadrant of <math id="S11.p21.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> with vertices <math id="S11.p21.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(0,0)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(0,0)</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S11.p21.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(A,0)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(A,0)</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="S11.p21.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(0,A)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(0,A)</annotation></semantics></math>. Let</span></p>
<table id="S11.Ex37" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S11.Ex37.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{\operatorname{int}(T)}\coloneqq\left\{(z_{1},z_{2})\in\mathbb{C}^{2}\mid\pi(|z_{1}|^{2},|z_{2}|^{2})\in\operatorname{int}(T)\right\}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>int</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℂ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>int</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{\operatorname{int}(T)}\coloneqq\left\{(z_{1},z_{2})\in\mathbb{C}^{2}\mid\pi(|z_{1}|^{2},|z_{2}|^{2})\in\operatorname{int}(T)\right\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S11.p21.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S11.p21.3.1" class="ltx_text">denote the toric domain associated to the interior of <math id="S11.p21.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math>. It is well-known that the interior of <math id="S11.p21.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B(A)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B(A)</annotation></semantics></math> symplectically embeds into <math id="S11.p21.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{\operatorname{int}(T)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>int</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{\operatorname{int}(T)}</annotation></semantics></math>, see e.g. <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bibx84" title="" class="ltx_ref">Tra95</a>]</cite>. The claim follows in view of the symplectomorphism</span></p>
<table id="S11.Ex38" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S11.Ex38.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W\rightarrow X_{\operatorname{int}(T)}\qquad(s,t,re^{2\pi i\theta})\mapsto\left(\sqrt{\frac{s}{\pi}}e^{2\pi it},\sqrt{1-r^{2}}e^{-2\pi i\theta}\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>int</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><mspace style="width:2em;" width="2em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msqrt><mfrac><mi>s</mi><mi>π</mi></mfrac></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W\rightarrow X_{\operatorname{int}(T)}\qquad(s,t,re^{2\pi i\theta})\mapsto\left(\sqrt{\frac{s}{\pi}}e^{2\pi it},\sqrt{1-r^{2}}e^{-2\pi i\theta}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S11.p22" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S11.p22.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S11.p22.1.1" class="ltx_text">It remains to show that every compact subset <math id="S11.p22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> of the interior of <math id="S11.p22.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X(H)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X(H)</annotation></semantics></math> admits a symplectic embedding into <math id="S11.p22.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U(H)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U(H)</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="S11.p22.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L\subset\mathbb{C}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⊂</mo><msup><mi>ℂ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L\subset\mathbb{C}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the complex axis <math id="S11.p22.m5" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\left\{z_{1}=0\right\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>{</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\{z_{1}=0\right\}</annotation></semantics></math>. By construction, <math id="S11.p22.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U(H)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U(H)</annotation></semantics></math> is symplectomorphic to <math id="S11.p22.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{int}(X(H))\setminus L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>int</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∖</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{int}(X(H))\setminus L</annotation></semantics></math>. This means that if we can find a compactly supported symplectomorphism <math id="S11.p22.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>φ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="S11.p22.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{int}(X(H))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>int</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{int}(X(H))</annotation></semantics></math> which disjoins <math id="S11.p22.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math> from <math id="S11.p22.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="S11.p22.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> symplectically embeds into <math id="S11.p22.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U(H)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U(H)</annotation></semantics></math>. One can construct <math id="S11.p22.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>φ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi</annotation></semantics></math> as follows: Consider the <math id="S11.p22.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>3</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3</annotation></semantics></math>-dimensional half space <math id="S11.p22.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q\coloneqq\mathbb{R}_{\geq 0}\times\mathbb{C}\subset\mathbb{C}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>≔</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>ℂ</mi></mrow><mo>⊂</mo><msup><mi>ℂ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q\coloneqq\mathbb{R}_{\geq 0}\times\mathbb{C}\subset\mathbb{C}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>. The boundary of <math id="S11.p22.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q</annotation></semantics></math> is precisely <math id="S11.p22.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math> and the intersection of <math id="S11.p22.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="S11.p22.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X(H)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X(H)</annotation></semantics></math> is of the form <math id="S11.p22.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left\{(g(z),z)\mid z\in\mathbb{D}\right\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>𝔻</mi></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\{(g(z),z)\mid z\in\mathbb{D}\right\}</annotation></semantics></math> for a suitable function <math id="S11.p22.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g:\mathbb{D}\rightarrow\mathbb{R}_{\geq 0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>𝔻</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g:\mathbb{D}\rightarrow\mathbb{R}_{\geq 0}</annotation></semantics></math>. The leaves of the characteristic foliation on <math id="S11.p22.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q</annotation></semantics></math> induced by the symplectic form are rays of the form <math id="S11.p22.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}_{\geq 0}\times\left\{*\right\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∗</mo><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}_{\geq 0}\times\left\{*\right\}</annotation></semantics></math>. Now consider an isotopy of <math id="S11.p22.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math> supported inside <math id="S11.p22.m26" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{int}(X(H))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>int</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{int}(X(H))</annotation></semantics></math> which pushes <math id="S11.p22.m27" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math> along the characteristic rays on <math id="S11.p22.m28" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q</annotation></semantics></math> towards the boundary of <math id="S11.p22.m29" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X(H)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X(H)</annotation></semantics></math>. Any such isotopy can be realized by a Hamiltonian flow compactly supported in the interior of <math id="S11.p22.m30" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X(H)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X(H)</annotation></semantics></math> and it is clearly possible to disjoin <math id="S11.p22.m31" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math> from <math id="S11.p22.m32" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> via such an isotopy. This concludes the proof of the lemma.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S11.p23" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S11.p23.1" class="ltx_p">We are finally in a position to prove Proposition <a href="#S11.Thmtheorem2" title="Proposition 11.2. ‣ 11. 𝐶^{2-𝜀} failure of packing stability ‣ Packing stability and the subleading asymptotics of symplectic Weyl laws" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">11.2</span></a>, i.e. that the error terms <math id="S11.p23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e_{k}^{\operatorname{alt}}(X(H))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>e</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>alt</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e_{k}^{\operatorname{alt}}(X(H))</annotation></semantics></math> diverge to <math id="S11.p23.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-\infty</annotation></semantics></math> as <math id="S11.p23.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> tends to <math id="S11.p23.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\infty</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S11.6" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof of Proposition <a href="#S11.Thmtheorem2" title="Proposition 11.2. ‣ 11. 𝐶^{2-𝜀} failure of packing stability ‣ Packing stability and the subleading asymptotics of symplectic Weyl laws" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">11.2</span></a>.</h6>
<div id="S11.p24" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S11.p24.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S11.p24.1.1" class="ltx_text">It follows from Lemma <a href="#S11.Thmtheorem9" title="Lemma 11.9. ‣ 11. 𝐶^{2-𝜀} failure of packing stability ‣ Packing stability and the subleading asymptotics of symplectic Weyl laws" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">11.9</span></a> and <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bibx45" title="" class="ltx_ref">EH</a>, Lemma 5.2]</cite> that</span></p>
<table id="S11.E8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(11.8)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S11.E8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{e_{d}}(\operatorname{id}_{S^{2}},\gamma_{d},H+A)-c_{U^{k}e_{d}}(\operatorname{id}_{S^{2}},\gamma_{d},0)+\int_{\gamma_{d}}(H+A)dt\geq c_{k}^{\operatorname{alt}}(X(H)\sqcup B(A))" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>id</mi><msup><mi>S</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mrow><msup><mi>U</mi><mi>k</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>id</mi><msup><mi>S</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0em">∫</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></msub><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>alt</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⊔</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{e_{d}}(\operatorname{id}_{S^{2}},\gamma_{d},H+A)-c_{U^{k}e_{d}}(\operatorname{id}_{S^{2}},\gamma_{d},0)+\int_{\gamma_{d}}(H+A)dt\geq c_{k}^{\operatorname{alt}}(X(H)\sqcup B(A))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S11.p24.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S11.p24.2.1" class="ltx_text">for all <math id="S11.p24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>. Set <math id="S11.p24.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V\coloneqq\operatorname{vol}(M)=\int_{[0,1]\times S^{2}}(H+A)dt\wedge\omega" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mi>vol</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0em">∫</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></msub><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>∧</mo><mi>ω</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V\coloneqq\operatorname{vol}(M)=\int_{[0,1]\times S^{2}}(H+A)dt\wedge\omega</annotation></semantics></math>. Moreover, abbreviate</span></p>
<table id="S11.Ex39" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S11.Ex39.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n_{d}\coloneqq\left\lfloor\frac{d^{2}V}{A^{2}(d+1)}\right\rfloor\qquad\text{and}\qquad k_{d}\coloneqq n_{d}(d+1)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mo>⌊</mo><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>⌋</mo></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:2em;" width="2em"></mspace><mtext>and</mtext><mspace style="width:2em;" width="2em"></mspace><mrow><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo>≔</mo><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n_{d}\coloneqq\left\lfloor\frac{d^{2}V}{A^{2}(d+1)}\right\rfloor\qquad\text{and}\qquad k_{d}\coloneqq n_{d}(d+1).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S11.p24.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S11.p24.3.1" class="ltx_text">Since our underlying surface is the sphere <math id="S11.p24.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>S</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, every PFH class <math id="S11.p24.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="S11.p24.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>U</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U</annotation></semantics></math>-cyclic of order <math id="S11.p24.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math>. Combining inequality (<a href="#S11.E8" title="In Proof of Proposition . ‣ 11. 𝐶^{2-𝜀} failure of packing stability ‣ Packing stability and the subleading asymptotics of symplectic Weyl laws" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">11.8</span></a>) with <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bibx45" title="" class="ltx_ref">EH</a>, Proposition 4.2(a)]</cite>, we see that</span></p>
<table id="S11.Ex40" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S11.Ex40.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{e_{d}}(\operatorname{id}_{S^{2}},\gamma_{d},H+A)-c_{e_{d}}(\operatorname{id}_{S^{2}},\gamma_{d},0)+\int_{\gamma_{d}}(H+A)dt\geq c_{k_{d}}^{\operatorname{alt}}(X(H)\sqcup B(A))-n_{d}A." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>id</mi><msup><mi>S</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>id</mi><msup><mi>S</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0em">∫</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></msub><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>c</mi><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mi>alt</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⊔</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{e_{d}}(\operatorname{id}_{S^{2}},\gamma_{d},H+A)-c_{e_{d}}(\operatorname{id}_{S^{2}},\gamma_{d},0)+\int_{\gamma_{d}}(H+A)dt\geq c_{k_{d}}^{\operatorname{alt}}(X(H)\sqcup B(A))-n_{d}A.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S11.p24.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="S11.p24.4.1" class="ltx_text">Set</span></p>
<table id="S11.Ex41" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S11.Ex41.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i_{d}\coloneqq\left\lfloor\frac{\operatorname{vol}(X(H))k_{d}}{V}\right\rfloor\qquad\text{and}\qquad j_{d}\coloneqq k_{d}-i_{d}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mo>⌊</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>vol</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow><mi>V</mi></mfrac><mo>⌋</mo></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:2em;" width="2em"></mspace><mtext>and</mtext><mspace style="width:2em;" width="2em"></mspace><mrow><msub><mi>j</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo>≔</mo><mrow><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i_{d}\coloneqq\left\lfloor\frac{\operatorname{vol}(X(H))k_{d}}{V}\right\rfloor\qquad\text{and}\qquad j_{d}\coloneqq k_{d}-i_{d}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S11.p24.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="S11.p24.5.1" class="ltx_text">By the disjoint union property for the capacities <math id="S11.p24.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{k}^{\operatorname{alt}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>alt</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{k}^{\operatorname{alt}}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</span></p>
<table id="S11.Ex42" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S11.Ex42.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{k_{d}}^{\operatorname{alt}}(X(H)\sqcup B(A))\geq c_{i_{d}}^{\operatorname{alt}}(X(H))+c_{j_{d}}^{\operatorname{alt}}(B(A))=2\sqrt{\operatorname{vol}(X(H))i_{d}}+2\sqrt{\operatorname{vol}(B(A))j_{d}}+e_{i_{d}}^{\operatorname{alt}}(X(H))+O(1)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>c</mi><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mi>alt</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⊔</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>c</mi><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mi>alt</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>c</mi><msub><mi>j</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mi>alt</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mrow><mi>vol</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mrow><mi>vol</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>j</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>e</mi><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mi>alt</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{k_{d}}^{\operatorname{alt}}(X(H)\sqcup B(A))\geq c_{i_{d}}^{\operatorname{alt}}(X(H))+c_{j_{d}}^{\operatorname{alt}}(B(A))=2\sqrt{\operatorname{vol}(X(H))i_{d}}+2\sqrt{\operatorname{vol}(B(A))j_{d}}+e_{i_{d}}^{\operatorname{alt}}(X(H))+O(1)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S11.p24.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="S11.p24.6.1" class="ltx_text">An elementary computation shows that</span></p>
<table id="S11.Ex43" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S11.Ex43.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2\sqrt{\operatorname{vol}(X(H))i_{d}}+2\sqrt{\operatorname{vol}(B(A))j_{d}}-n_{d}A=dA^{-1}V+O(1)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mrow><mi>vol</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mrow><mi>vol</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>j</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2\sqrt{\operatorname{vol}(X(H))i_{d}}+2\sqrt{\operatorname{vol}(B(A))j_{d}}-n_{d}A=dA^{-1}V+O(1).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S11.p24.7" class="ltx_p"><span id="S11.p24.7.1" class="ltx_text">We deduce that</span></p>
<table id="S11.E9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(11.9)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S11.E9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{e_{d}}(\operatorname{id}_{S^{2}},\gamma_{d},H+A)-c_{e_{d}}(\operatorname{id}_{S^{2}},\gamma_{d},0)+\int_{\gamma_{d}}(H+A)dt-dA^{-1}V\geq e_{i_{d}}^{\operatorname{alt}}(X(H))+O(1)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>id</mi><msup><mi>S</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>id</mi><msup><mi>S</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0em">∫</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></msub><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>e</mi><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mi>alt</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{e_{d}}(\operatorname{id}_{S^{2}},\gamma_{d},H+A)-c_{e_{d}}(\operatorname{id}_{S^{2}},\gamma_{d},0)+\int_{\gamma_{d}}(H+A)dt-dA^{-1}V\geq e_{i_{d}}^{\operatorname{alt}}(X(H))+O(1).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S11.p24.8" class="ltx_p"><span id="S11.p24.8.1" class="ltx_text">Using <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bibx45" title="" class="ltx_ref">EH</a>, Remark 4.4]</cite> and Lemma <a href="#S11.Thmtheorem8" title="Lemma 11.8. ‣ 11. 𝐶^{2-𝜀} failure of packing stability ‣ Packing stability and the subleading asymptotics of symplectic Weyl laws" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">11.8</span></a>, we see that</span></p>
<table id="S11.p24.9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S11.p24.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{e_{d}}(\operatorname{id}_{S^{2}},\gamma_{d},H+A)+\int_{\gamma_{d}}(H+A)dt-dA^{-1}V\\
=c_{e_{d}}(\operatorname{id}_{S^{2}},\gamma_{d},H)+\int_{\gamma_{d}}Hdt-dA^{-1}\int_{[0,1]\times S^{2}}Hdt\wedge\omega\quad\longrightarrow\quad-\infty\qquad(d\rightarrow\infty)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>id</mi><msup><mi>S</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0em">∫</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></msub><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>c</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>id</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><msup><mi>S</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>d</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mo>∫</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></msub><mi>H</mi><mi>d</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>d</mi><mi>A</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>∫</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></msub><mi>H</mi><mi>d</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>∧</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo lspace="1.278em" rspace="0.778em" stretchy="false">⟶</mo><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo lspace="2.000em" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{e_{d}}(\operatorname{id}_{S^{2}},\gamma_{d},H+A)+\int_{\gamma_{d}}(H+A)dt-dA^{-1}V\\
=c_{e_{d}}(\operatorname{id}_{S^{2}},\gamma_{d},H)+\int_{\gamma_{d}}Hdt-dA^{-1}\int_{[0,1]\times S^{2}}Hdt\wedge\omega\quad\longrightarrow\quad-\infty\qquad(d\rightarrow\infty).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S11.p24.10" class="ltx_p"><span id="S11.p24.10.1" class="ltx_text">Moreover, as already observed in the proof of Theorem <a href="#Thmintrothm6" title="Theorem F (Subleading asymptotics link spectral invariants). ‣ 1.4. Subleading asymptotics of symplectic Weyl laws ‣ 1. Introduction ‣ Packing stability and the subleading asymptotics of symplectic Weyl laws" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">F</span></a>, the spectral invariant <math id="S11.p24.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{e_{d}}(\operatorname{id}_{S^{2}},\gamma_{d},0)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>id</mi><msup><mi>S</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{e_{d}}(\operatorname{id}_{S^{2}},\gamma_{d},0)</annotation></semantics></math> vanishes. Combining these observations with inequality (<a href="#S11.E9" title="In Proof of Proposition . ‣ 11. 𝐶^{2-𝜀} failure of packing stability ‣ Packing stability and the subleading asymptotics of symplectic Weyl laws" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">11.9</span></a>), we see that <math id="S11.p24.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e_{i_{d}}^{\operatorname{alt}}(X(H))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>e</mi><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mi>alt</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e_{i_{d}}^{\operatorname{alt}}(X(H))</annotation></semantics></math> tends to <math id="S11.p24.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-\infty</annotation></semantics></math> as <math id="S11.p24.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math> goes to infinity. From this one can further deduce that the entire sequence of error terms <math id="S11.p24.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e_{k}^{\operatorname{alt}}(X(H))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>e</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>alt</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e_{k}^{\operatorname{alt}}(X(H))</annotation></semantics></math> diverges to <math id="S11.p24.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-\infty</annotation></semantics></math>. Indeed, since the sequence <math id="S11.p24.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{k}^{\operatorname{alt}}(X(H))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>alt</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{k}^{\operatorname{alt}}(X(H))</annotation></semantics></math> is non-decreasing in <math id="S11.p24.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</span></p>
<table id="S11.Ex44" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S11.Ex44.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e_{k}^{\operatorname{alt}}(X(H))-e_{\ell}^{\operatorname{alt}}(X(H))\leq 2\sqrt{\operatorname{vol}(X(H))}(\sqrt{k}-\sqrt{\ell})\qquad\text{for all $k\geq\ell$}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>e</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>alt</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>e</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>alt</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>vol</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msqrt><mi>k</mi></msqrt><mo>−</mo><msqrt><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msqrt></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:2em;" width="2em"></mspace><mrow><mtext>for all </mtext><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≥</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e_{k}^{\operatorname{alt}}(X(H))-e_{\ell}^{\operatorname{alt}}(X(H))\leq 2\sqrt{\operatorname{vol}(X(H))}(\sqrt{k}-\sqrt{\ell})\qquad\text{for all $k\geq\ell$}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S11.p24.11" class="ltx_p"><span id="S11.p24.11.1" class="ltx_text">Since <math id="S11.p24.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i_{d}</annotation></semantics></math> grows quadratically in <math id="S11.p24.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math>, this estimate is enough to control all error terms <math id="S11.p24.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e_{k}^{\operatorname{alt}}(X(H))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>e</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>alt</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e_{k}^{\operatorname{alt}}(X(H))</annotation></semantics></math> just in terms of the subsequence <math id="S11.p24.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e_{i_{d}}^{\operatorname{alt}}(X(H))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>e</mi><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mi>alt</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e_{i_{d}}^{\operatorname{alt}}(X(H))</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
